    "num_matrix_float_is_symmetric" => "Validated portable Matrix specialization. Format/version, dense rank/shape, indices, finite values and allocation limits are checked. Real specializes exact rational arithmetic and permits only Native backend. Backend changes are immutable. Determinants return normalized magnitude, entry_unit and order, representing normalized*entry_unit^order; packed LU similarly operates on entries normalized by one canonical input unit. RREF/null-space vectors are dimensionless. No pointer or process-local handle is serialized. Checks if the matrix is symmetric (\$A = A^T\$).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_matrix_float_jacobi_eigen_decomposition" => "Validated portable Matrix specialization. Format/version, dense rank/shape, indices, finite values and allocation limits are checked. Real specializes exact rational arithmetic and permits only Native backend. Backend changes are immutable. Determinants return normalized magnitude, entry_unit and order, representing normalized*entry_unit^order; packed LU similarly operates on entries normalized by one canonical input unit. RREF/null-space vectors are dimensionless. No pointer or process-local handle is serialized. Finds the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of a symmetric matrix using the Jacobi iteration method. The Jacobi method is an iterative algorithm for computing the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of a real symmetric matrix by performing a sequence of orthogonal similarity transformations. # Arguments * `max_sweeps` - The maximum number of sweeps (iterations) to perform. * `tolerance` - The convergence tolerance for off-diagonal elements. # Returns A `Result` containing a tuple `(eigenvalues, eigenvectors)` where `eigenvalues` is a `Vec<f64>` and `eigenvectors` is a `Matrix<f64>` (columns are eigenvectors). # Errors Returns an error if: - The matrix is not square. - The decomposition fails to converge within the maximum sweeps.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
