    "num_matrix_float_lu_decomposition" => "Validated portable Matrix specialization. Format/version, dense rank/shape, indices, finite values and allocation limits are checked. Real specializes exact rational arithmetic and permits only Native backend. Backend changes are immutable. Determinants return normalized magnitude, entry_unit and order, representing normalized*entry_unit^order; packed LU similarly operates on entries normalized by one canonical input unit. RREF/null-space vectors are dimensionless. No pointer or process-local handle is serialized. Computes the LU decomposition of a square matrix. # Returns A tuple containing the LU matrix and the number of row swaps. # Errors Returns an error if: - The matrix is not square. - The matrix is singular.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_matrix_float_mul_strassen" => "Validated portable Matrix specialization. Format/version, dense rank/shape, indices, finite values and allocation limits are checked. Real specializes exact rational arithmetic and permits only Native backend. Backend changes are immutable. Determinants return normalized magnitude, entry_unit and order, representing normalized*entry_unit^order; packed LU similarly operates on entries normalized by one canonical input unit. RREF/null-space vectors are dimensionless. No pointer or process-local handle is serialized. # Strassen's Matrix Multiplication This function multiplies two matrices using Strassen's algorithm, which is more efficient for large matrices than the naive O(n^3) algorithm. ## Arguments * `other` - The matrix to multiply with. ## Returns A new `Matrix` representing the product of the two matrices. ## Errors Returns an error if: - Matrix multiplication is not possible due to incompatible dimensions. - The matrices are not square (for the internal recursive calls).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
