    "num_matrix_float_null_space" => "Validated portable Matrix specialization. Format/version, dense rank/shape, indices, finite values and allocation limits are checked. Real specializes exact rational arithmetic and permits only Native backend. Backend changes are immutable. Determinants return normalized magnitude, entry_unit and order, representing normalized*entry_unit^order; packed LU similarly operates on entries normalized by one canonical input unit. RREF/null-space vectors are dimensionless. No pointer or process-local handle is serialized. Computes a basis for the null space (kernel) of the matrix. The null space of a matrix `A` is the set of all vectors `x` such that `Ax = 0`. This method finds the null space by first computing the RREF of the matrix, identifying pivot and free variables, and then constructing basis vectors. # Returns A `Matrix` whose columns form a basis for the null space. # Errors Returns an error if the RREF calculation fails.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
