    "num_matrix_real_inverse" => "Validated portable Matrix specialization. Format/version, dense rank/shape, indices, finite values and allocation limits are checked. Real specializes exact rational arithmetic and permits only Native backend. Backend changes are immutable. Determinants return normalized magnitude, entry_unit and order, representing normalized*entry_unit^order; packed LU similarly operates on entries normalized by one canonical input unit. RREF/null-space vectors are dimensionless. No pointer or process-local handle is serialized. Computes the inverse of a square matrix. This method uses Gaussian elimination on an augmented matrix `[A | I]` to transform `A` into the identity matrix `I`, resulting in `[I | A^-1]`. # Returns * `Some(Matrix)` containing the inverse matrix if it exists. * `None` if the matrix is not square or is singular (not invertible).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
