    "num_native_cubic_spline_d1" => "Portable native approximation model with independent coordinate and ordinate dimensions. Every query checks kind/version, defining data lengths, finite data, monotone grids where required, interval and allocation budgets. Derivatives restore ordinate/coordinate powers; integrals restore their product. Model values contain only defining data and no process-local references. Derivative of order 1, 2 or 3 at `x` (order 0 is the value).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_cubic_spline_d2" => "Portable native approximation model with independent coordinate and ordinate dimensions. Every query checks kind/version, defining data lengths, finite data, monotone grids where required, interval and allocation budgets. Derivatives restore ordinate/coordinate powers; integrals restore their product. Model values contain only defining data and no process-local references. Derivative of order 1, 2 or 3 at `x` (order 0 is the value).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_cubic_spline_d3" => "Portable native approximation model with independent coordinate and ordinate dimensions. Every query checks kind/version, defining data lengths, finite data, monotone grids where required, interval and allocation budgets. Derivatives restore ordinate/coordinate powers; integrals restore their product. Model values contain only defining data and no process-local references. Derivative of order 1, 2 or 3 at `x` (order 0 is the value).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_cubic_spline_eval" => "Portable native approximation model with independent coordinate and ordinate dimensions. Every query checks kind/version, defining data lengths, finite data, monotone grids where required, interval and allocation budgets. Derivatives restore ordinate/coordinate powers; integrals restore their product. Model values contain only defining data and no process-local references. Spline value at `x` (extrapolates with the end cubics).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_cubic_spline_integrate" => "Portable native approximation model with independent coordinate and ordinate dimensions. Every query checks kind/version, defining data lengths, finite data, monotone grids where required, interval and allocation budgets. Derivatives restore ordinate/coordinate powers; integrals restore their product. Model values contain only defining data and no process-local references. Exact integral of the spline over `[lo, hi]`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_cubic_spline_new" => "Portable native approximation model with independent coordinate and ordinate dimensions. Every query checks kind/version, defining data lengths, finite data, monotone grids where required, interval and allocation budgets. Derivatives restore ordinate/coordinate powers; integrals restore their product. Model values contain only defining data and no process-local references. Builds an interpolating spline through `(x, y)`. # Errors [`ApproxError::Invalid`] for fewer than 3 points (4 for not-a-knot) non-increasing abscissae, or non-finite data or clamped derivatives; [`ApproxError::Singular`] if the system overflows or cannot be solved.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_curl_scaled" => "Native finite-difference calculus with physical reference scales: point,coordinate_scale,value_scale,max_evaluations,[partial index or Jacobian output count],callback. Independent D/E units; derivative E/D, Hessian/Laplacian E/D^2. References are positive. Shared callback errors and finite evaluation budgets are preserved. Curl of a three-dimensional vector field. Returns `None` for wrong dimensions.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_damped_harmonic_oscillator" => "Actual native damped oscillator. Amplitude/result retain an arbitrary physical domain; angular frequency and damping have inverse-Time units, phase is dimensionless, elapsed time is Time. Damped harmonic oscillator solution. Returns position for underdamped case: x(t) = A * e^(-γt) * cos(ω't + φ) where ω' = √(ω₀² - γ²) # Arguments * `amplitude` - Initial amplitude * `omega0` - Natural angular frequency ω₀ * `gamma` - Damping coefficient γ * `phase` - Initial phase * `time` - Time\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_dd_abs" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Absolute value.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_dd_from_f64" => "Construct native double-double from a finite physical scalar; coherent values and physical dimensions are retained. Exact conversion from `f64`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_dd_from_parts" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Builds a normalised value from an unnormalised pair.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_dd_hypot" => "Computes the two-coordinate Euclidean norm at double-double precision. Both session-owned inputs must have the same physical dimension, which the retained result preserves. Euclidean norm of two double-double components. The inputs are scaled before squaring when needed. The result retains the low part unless the norm rounds to a subnormal or overflows.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_dd_is_finite" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Whether both parts are finite.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_dd_parts" => "Returns the high and low components as item0 and item1. Both have the physical dimension of the double-double input, and the low component is kept separately from the high one. Returns the stored high and low components without rounding their sum.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_dd_sqrt" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Square root with about 100 bits of precision. Negative inputs return NaN. Positive infinity returns infinity.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_dd_to_f64" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Rounds to the nearest `f64`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_derivative_scaled" => "Native finite-difference calculus with physical reference scales: point,coordinate_scale,value_scale,max_evaluations,[partial index or Jacobian output count],callback. Independent D/E units; derivative E/D, Hessian/Laplacian E/D^2. References are positive. Shared callback errors and finite evaluation budgets are preserved. Central-difference derivative of `f` at `x`.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_device_alloc" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_analyse_extra" => "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. Validates the program and returns the type and phase of every register. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`].\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_array_matmul" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. `c = a * b` for row-major `a` (`m x k`), `b` (`k x n`), `c` (`m x n`), through [`matmul_kernel`]. This is what a device without a tuned `matmul` of its own uses. # Errors [`DeviceError::Mismatch`] on wrong sizes; any error of the launch.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_array_reduce" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Reduces a whole one-column buffer on the device (see [`reduce_column`]). # Errors As [`reduce_column`].\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_backend" => "Explicit native backend specialization. Feature-disabled JIT/GPU builds return Unsupported; machine representations are normalized and source, row, fold-work and allocation budgets are checked. A backend executing on `device`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_backend_eval" => "Explicit native backend specialization. Feature-disabled JIT/GPU builds return Unsupported; machine representations are normalized and source, row, fold-work and allocation budgets are checked.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_backend_name" => "Explicit native backend specialization. Feature-disabled JIT/GPU builds return Unsupported; machine representations are normalized and source, row, fold-work and allocation budgets are checked.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_buffer_dtype" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Element type.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_buffer_is_empty" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Whether the buffer has no elements.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_buffer_len" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Number of elements.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_buffer_new_extra" => "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. Wraps device storage. For [`Device`] implementors.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_buffer_owner" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The [`DeviceInfo`]-independent unique number of the owning device.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_buffer_storage_extra" => "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. The device-private storage.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_buffer_storage_mut_extra" => "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. The device-private storage, mutably.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_build_devices" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The device kinds this *build* can offer, as [`DeviceKind::tag`]s. A compile-time fact (it does not probe hardware), so it can go in the kernel manifest. `gpu-wgpu` here means the build can drive GPUs; whether one is present is answered by `registry().list()`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_builder_finish" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Finishes with the given outputs. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when the result does not validate.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_builder_finish_fold" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Finishes a program with a loop. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when the result does not validate.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_builder_idx" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. An index constant.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_builder_is_empty" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Whether no instruction was pushed yet.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_builder_len" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Number of instructions so far.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_builder_new" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. A builder for a kernel with the given input and parameter counts.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_builder_num" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. A numeric constant.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_builder_push" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Appends an operation and returns its register (leaves are shared).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_builder_splice" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Splices `other` into this program with its input `i` bound to `inputs[i]` and its parameter `j` to `params[j]`; returns its outputs. `other` must not use `gather` (it addresses the caller's columns) and its own fold, if any, is not carried over: splice elementwise programs.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_check_copy" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Checks the arguments of a [`Device::copy`]. For implementors. # Errors [`DeviceError::Mismatch`].\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_check_launch" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Checks the buffers and sizes of a launch. For implementors. # Errors [`DeviceError::Mismatch`].\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_check_launch_cols" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Checks the buffers and sizes of a [`Device::launch_cols`]. For implementors. # Errors [`DeviceError::Mismatch`]; [`DeviceError::Unsupported`] when a length does not fit the 32-bit indices every device shares.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_cmp" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. A comparison as `1.0` / `0.0` (`!=` is true for NaN operands).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_column_get_extra" => "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. Element `index` of column `col`, NaN when either is out of range.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_column_offsets" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Prefix sums of column lengths: the offsets of a column-major buffer.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_compile" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_compiled_as_any" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_compiled_ir" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_copy" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_cpu" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The single-threaded device (`cpu`).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_cpu_parallel" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The rayon device (`cpu-parallel`).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_dopri" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. One attempted Dormand-Prince 5(4) step per row, with per-row time and step size. Inputs: the `n_state` state columns, then `t`, then `h`. Parameters: those of `rhs`, then `t_end` and `t_done` (the time from which a row counts as finished), then `rtol` and `atol`. Outputs: the same `n_state + 2` columns after the attempt. A row whose error estimate is within tolerance advances; any other keeps its state and retries with a smaller step; a finished row is left untouched. No row waits for another. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when `rhs` is not an ODE right-hand side for `n_state` variables (see [`super::rk4_step`]).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_download" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_ds_join" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The `f64` a pair stands for.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_ds_split" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The pair `(hi, lo)` of an `f64`: `hi` is the nearest `f32`, `lo` the nearest `f32` to the remainder.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_dtype_epsilon" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Epsilon used for tolerances on the device: `2^-23` for `F32`, `2^-52` for native `F64` and `2^-44` for double-single emulation.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_emit" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Emits `ir` for the target in `options`. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when `ir` does not validate or the workgroup size is zero; [`DeviceError::Unsupported`] when the target has no type of the requested precision.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_emit_ds" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Emits the double-single WGSL module for `ir`. The bindings are those of [`super::emit`] with `array<vec2<f32>>` for `rssn_in`, `rssn_params` and `rssn_out`. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when `ir` does not validate or the workgroup size is zero.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_emit_wgsl" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Emits the WGSL module. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when `ir` does not validate or the workgroup size is zero.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_emitter_emit" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_emitter_target" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_ensemble_dopri5_extra" => "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. Integrates `y' = f([t,] y; params)` from `t0` to `t1 > t0` for many initial conditions at once with adaptive Dormand-Prince 5(4) steps. Every trajectory carries its own time and step size on the device ([`dopri5_step`]), so a stiff row takes small steps while the others take large ones. The host only asks, every few launches, for the minimum of the time column ([`reduce_column`]): one number crosses per check. The result for a row does not depend on the rest of the batch. # Errors Any [`DeviceError`]; [`DeviceError::Mismatch`] for `t1 < t0`, a wrong parameter count or ragged initial conditions; [`DeviceError::Backend`] when some trajectory has not arrived after `tolerance.max_launches` launches (a blow-up, or a tolerance the float type cannot meet).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_ensemble_rk4_extra" => "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. Integrates `y' = f([t,] y; params)` for many initial conditions at once with fixed-step RK4, entirely through [`Device::launch`]. `y0[i][row]` is state variable `i` of trajectory `row`. Returns the states at `t1` in the same layout. The step kernel ([`rk4_step`]) is compiled once; each of the `steps` launches advances every trajectory by `(t1 - t0) / steps`. Trajectories are independent, so the result for a row does not depend on the rest of the batch. # Errors Any [`DeviceError`]; [`DeviceError::Mismatch`] for `steps == 0`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_eval_at_extra" => "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. Reference evaluation of row `row` of a launch of `rows` rows over `cols`: the semantics of the whole IR, fold included. `analysis` must come from [`KernelIr::analyse`] of this program; `out` receives one value per output.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_gather_slot" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The input column a gather reads, or `None` when the index is not finite, is negative, or points past the declared inputs.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_gpu_new" => "Explicit native backend specialization. Feature-disabled JIT/GPU builds return Unsupported; machine representations are normalized and source, row, fold-work and allocation budgets are checked. Opens `adapter`. # Errors [`DeviceError::Backend`] when the device cannot be created.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_gpu_probe" => "Explicit native backend specialization. Feature-disabled JIT/GPU builds return Unsupported; machine representations are normalized and source, row, fold-work and allocation budgets are checked. Every usable wgpu adapter, as devices `gpu:wgpu:0`, `gpu:wgpu:1`, ... Software rasterisers (CPU adapters) are included and marked in the name.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_info" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_kernel_analyse" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Validates the program and returns the type and phase of every register. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`].\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_kernel_eval" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Reference evaluation of one row of an elementwise launch (the semantics every device must reproduce, up to its precision): `inputs` holds that row's element of every column. Slow; for tests and fallbacks. A malformed program evaluates to NaN.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_kernel_from_tape" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Lowers a tape. # Errors [`DeviceError::Unsupported`] when the tape contains a host call (`Call`, `Extern1`, `Extern2`); [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when it is malformed.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_kernel_is_elementwise" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Whether the program is in the elementwise core: no fold and only tape instructions.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_kernel_structural_hash" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. A structural hash (constants by bit pattern): the key under which a device caches its compiled form.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_kernel_validate" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Checks SSA order, index ranges, register types and phases. Every device calls this before it runs or emits a program, so a malformed program cannot index outside a register file or a buffer. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`].\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_kind" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. A short stable tag: `cpu`, `cpu-parallel`, `gpu-wgpu`, `gpu-cuda`...\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_launch" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_launch_cols" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_literal" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. A WGSL `f32` expression for a constant.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_map_columns" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Upload, launch, download: `columns[i][row]` in, one vector per output out. The simple path; hold [`Buffer`]s yourself to keep data on the device between launches. # Errors Any [`DeviceError`].\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_map_physical" => "Execute the actual native device kernel with heterogeneous measured input columns, parameters and output units from a retained tape reference frame.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_map_reduce_extra" => "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. `op` over every output of `map` applied to `columns`, fused: one value per output of `map`, and no mapped column is ever stored. # Errors Any [`DeviceError`]; [`DeviceError::Mismatch`] when the columns differ in length or number.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_map_reduce_pass" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The first pass of a fused map-reduce. `map` (elementwise, any number of inputs and outputs) is evaluated inside the reduction block and each of its outputs is combined with `op`. The mapped columns never exist. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when `map` is not elementwise or uses `gather`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_matmul" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_matmul_kernel" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. `C = A * B` for row-major `A` (`m x k`, column 0) and `B` (`k x n`, column 1), one row of the launch per element of `C` (`m * n` rows). Parameter 0 is `n`; `k` follows from the length of `B`. # Errors Never in practice; the kernel is fixed.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_native_compile" => "Explicit native backend specialization. Feature-disabled JIT/GPU builds return Unsupported; machine representations are normalized and source, row, fold-work and allocation budgets are checked. Lowers and compiles `ir`; `None` when either step fails.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_native_lower" => "Explicit native backend specialization. Feature-disabled JIT/GPU builds return Unsupported; machine representations are normalized and source, row, fold-work and allocation budgets are checked. Lowers `ir` (with its analysis) to the LIR kernel described in the module documentation; `None` for kernels LIR cannot express.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_native_run" => "Explicit native backend specialization. Feature-disabled JIT/GPU builds return Unsupported; machine representations are normalized and source, row, fold-work and allocation budgets are checked. Runs rows `row_lo .. row_lo + out[0].len()`; `false` when the code bailed (the caller then interprets the launch).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_next_uid" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. A fresh owner number for a [`Buffer`]'s device. Each device instance takes one at construction.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_num_to_idx" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. A number truncated to an index: NaN gives `0`, the range saturates at the 32-bit limits every device shares.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_op_compare" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_op_is_elementwise" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Whether this is an instruction of the elementwise core (a tape instruction).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_op_map" => "Explicit finite register-map specialization of the native generic operand mapper. The same instruction with every operand register renamed by `m`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_op_new" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_op_operand_ty" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The type each operand must have.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_op_operands" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The operand registers (at most three) and how many are used.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_op_ty" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The type of the value this instruction defines (`select` takes the type of its branches, which [`KernelIr::analyse`] resolves; here it reports a number).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_op_unary" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_options_new" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The defaults for `target`: `f32`, workgroups of 64, entry `main` (`rssn_main` where `main` is reserved).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_options_precision" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The same options with another precision.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_pack_columns" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Packs columns into one column-major host vector. # Errors [`DeviceError::Mismatch`] when the columns differ in length.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_pairwise_kernel_extra" => "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. An all-pairs interaction over `columns` attribute columns. `pair` is elementwise with `2 * columns` inputs, the attributes of body `i` followed by those of body `j`, and any number of outputs; output `k` of the result is the `op`-combination over every `j` of output `k` of `pair`. With `skip_self` the term `j == i` is left out. The attributes of body `i` are loaded once per row, not once per pair. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when `pair` does not have that shape.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_plan_add_extra" => "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. Adds a kernel reading `inputs` (one source per input column of `ir`) with the uniform `params`. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when the kernel does not validate, the counts do not match, or a source names a later kernel, a missing output or a missing external column.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_plan_fuse_extra" => "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. Merges every producer into a consumer that reads it, as far as the rules in the module documentation allow. Returns the number of launches removed.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_plan_launches_extra" => "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. The number of launches [`Plan::run`] performs.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_plan_new_extra" => "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. A plan over `externals` input columns.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_plan_result_extra" => "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. Asks for `source` to be returned by [`Plan::run`] (results come back in the order they were asked for). # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] for a source that does not exist.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_plan_run_extra" => "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. Runs the plan on `device`: `externals[i]` is external column `i` (`rows` values each). Returns the requested results. # Errors [`DeviceError::Mismatch`] when a column has the wrong length or the count of externals is wrong; any error of the device.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_preferred_dtype" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. `F64` when the device has it, else `F32`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_reduce" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_reduce_column_extra" => "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. Reduces column `column` of `buffer`, whose columns have the lengths `lens`, to one number, on the device. Only the final value crosses to the host. An empty column gives the identity of `op`. # Errors Any [`DeviceError`]; [`DeviceError::Unsupported`] on a device without structured kernels.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_reduce_combine" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. `acc ∘ x`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_reduce_identity" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The neutral element.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_reduce_pass" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. One pass of a tree reduction over column `column` of a buffer with `inputs` columns: row `r` combines elements `r * FAN_IN ..` of that column. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when `column >= inputs`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_registry_default" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The device to use when the caller names none: the first GPU, else the parallel CPU with at least two workers, else the sequential CPU or any registered device.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_registry_empty" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. A registry with no devices.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_registry_first" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The first device of a kind.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_registry_get" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The device with this id.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_registry_global" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. The process-wide registry (created on first use).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_registry_list" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Descriptions of every device, in registration order.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_registry_new" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. A registry holding the built-in CPU devices (and, with feature `gpu-wgpu`, every adapter wgpu finds; none is not an error).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_registry_register" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Adds a device. # Errors [`DeviceError::Mismatch`] when the id is taken.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_rhs_shape" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Checks that `rhs` is an ODE right-hand side for `n_state` variables and reports whether it takes the time as input 0. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`].\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_rk4" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. One classical Runge-Kutta 4 step of `y' = f([t,] y)` as a kernel. `rhs` has `n_state` outputs and either `n_state` inputs (autonomous) or `n_state + 1` with the time as input 0. The step kernel has `n_state` inputs (the state columns of every trajectory), the parameters of `rhs` followed by two more, `t` at index `rhs.params` and the step `h` at `rhs.params + 1`, and `n_state` outputs (the next state). Launching it `steps` times with a changing `t` integrates every row, that is every initial condition, with the same program: the ODE-ensemble pattern. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when the shape of `rhs` does not match, or when `rhs` is not elementwise or uses `gather` (which addresses columns and cannot be composed).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_rk4_alias" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. One classical Runge-Kutta 4 step of `y' = f([t,] y)` as a kernel. `rhs` has `n_state` outputs and either `n_state` inputs (autonomous) or `n_state + 1` with the time as input 0. The step kernel has `n_state` inputs (the state columns of every trajectory), the parameters of `rhs` followed by two more, `t` at index `rhs.params` and the step `h` at `rhs.params + 1`, and `n_state` outputs (the next state). Launching it `steps` times with a changing `t` integrates every row, that is every initial condition, with the same program: the ODE-ensemble pattern. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when the shape of `rhs` does not match, or when `rhs` is not elementwise or uses `gather` (which addresses columns and cannot be composed).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_run_cols" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Launches `ir` over host columns of independent lengths and downloads the outputs, one vector per output column. # Errors Any [`DeviceError`].\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_select_is_true" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. `select` takes its first branch unless the condition is exactly zero.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_spmv_kernel" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. `y = A x` for a CSR matrix: column 0 the row pointers (`rows + 1` entries), column 1 the column indices, column 2 the values, column 3 the vector. One row of the launch per matrix row. Row pointers and column indices are stored as floats, so they are exact below `2^24` on an `f32` device (`2^53` on an `f64` one). # Errors Never in practice; the kernel is fixed.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_stencil1d_extra" => "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. A 1-D stencil: `out[r] = sum of weight * x[r + offset]` over `points`. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when `points` is empty or an offset does not fit 32 bits.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_stencil2d_extra" => "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. A 2-D stencil on a row-major `ny x nx` grid stored in one column. `out[y][x] = sum of weight * u[y + dy][x + dx]` over `points` (`(dx, dy, weight)`). Parameter 0 is `nx`; `ny` follows from the column length. The boundary rule applies per axis. # Errors [`DeviceError::InvalidKernel`] when `points` is empty or an offset does not fit 32 bits.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_storage_as_any_extra" => "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_storage_as_any_mut_extra" => "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_storage_new_extra" => "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_synchronize" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_target_has_f64" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. Whether the language has a 64-bit float.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_target_name" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution. A short name, also the extension of the golden files.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_to_tape_extra" => "Explicit native array/device object specialization. IR, buffer and generic storage values are normalized; physical programs retain their tape reference frame. Shapes and native execution work are bounded before launch. The same program as a tape (used by the reference checks), or `None` when it uses the structured extension, which a tape cannot express.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_uid" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_device_upload" => "Explicit checked native device adapter. Machine IR and buffers use normalized coordinates; use physical map for independently measured columns. Session, shape and bounded work are validated before native execution.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_differential_evolution_scaled" => "Native scaled global/constrained optimization with shared actual host evaluation limit. Nelder: x,xscale,yscale,step,tol,iterations,budget,f. Differential evolution: lo,hi,xscale,yscale,population,generations,budget,seed,f. Annealing: x,xscale,yscale,step,temperature,cooling,iterations,budget,seed,f. Constrained: x,xscale,yscale,equality_scale,inequality_scale,tol,iterations,budget,f,eq,ineq. Constraints independently carry C/H units; SQP returns physical multipliers E/C and E/H, native status and second-order verdict. Second-order: x,lambda,mu,xscale,yscale,eqscale,ineqscale,budget,f,eq,ineq. No global-optimality claim; native iteration/status semantics retained. Differential evolution (`rand/1/bin`) within box `bounds`, seeded.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_dirichlet_new" => "Construct the native dimensionless Dirichlet simplex distribution with positive concentration parameters.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_distribution_cdf" => "Native CDF of a sample quantity sharing the constructor reference domain. The cumulative distribution function at `x`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_distribution_mean" => "Native mean with sample units; mathematically undefined NaN moments report a domain error. The mean, when it exists.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_distribution_new" => "Construct a native distribution enum in normalized sample coordinates, then restore an explicit positive sample reference scale. All15 named variants are supported. Continuous density has inverse sample units; discrete probability mass remains dimensionless.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_distribution_pdf" => "Native normalized density restored by the explicit reference scale. For discrete variants this is probability mass and has no physical units. The probability density (or mass) at `x`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_distribution_quantile" => "Native inverse CDF restored to sample units. Valid infinite endpoint quantiles are preserved. The `u`-quantile, `0 ≤ u ≤ 1`: the inverse of [`Distribution::cdf`]. Closed-form inverses are used when available. Other continuous distributions invert the CDF by bracketed bisection, and discrete distributions search for the smallest supported count whose CDF reaches `u`. # Errors [`DistError::Domain`] when `u` is outside `[0, 1]` or a parameter is unusable.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_distribution_sample" => "Native FnMut uniform-source specialization using the shared session-owned Rng. Both distribution and random stream kinds are checked; result retains sample units. One sample, from a uniform source on `[0, 1)`. # Errors [`DistError::Domain`] for a parameter the sampler cannot use.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_distribution_variance" => "Native variance with squared sample units; undefined moments report an explicit domain error. The variance, when it exists.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_divergence_scaled" => "Native finite-difference calculus with physical reference scales: point,coordinate_scale,value_scale,max_evaluations,[partial index or Jacobian output count],callback. Independent D/E units; derivative E/D, Hessian/Laplacian E/D^2. References are positive. Shared callback errors and finite evaluation budgets are preserved. Divergence of a vector field, using central differences.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_dpd_density" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Number density.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_dpd_is_empty" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Whether there are no particles.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_dpd_len" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Number of particles.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_dpd_mean_velocity" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Mean velocity component `axis` over all particles.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_dpd_momentum" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Total momentum.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_dpd_new" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Random uniform positions and Maxwell velocities with zero total momentum. # Errors For a bad dimension, a box smaller than three cut-offs, or fewer than two particles.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_dpd_pressure" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Pressure `ρ k_B T_kin + (virial + wall virial) / (d V)` from the last force evaluation. The virial sums `Σ a w r` over interacting pairs plus `Σ f_wall d` over the particles within `r_c` of a wall, `d` being the distance to that wall. The result is the trace of the pressure tensor over `d`; a slab is not isotropic, so the normal and tangential pressures differ even though this single number does not say so.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_dpd_run" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Runs `steps` steps.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_dpd_set_walls" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Replaces the periodic boundary along `wall.axis` by a slab bounded by two walls at `0` and `L`. Particles outside are folded back and reflected; the wall force acts on later steps. Pair forces along that axis use the plain (not minimum-image) distance, and [`Dpd::pressure`] includes the virial of the wall force. Only one axis can be walled. # Errors For an axis outside the dimension, a negative `a_wall`, or a [`WallKind::NoSlip`] friction outside `[0, 1]`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_dpd_state" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_dpd_step" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. One modified velocity-Verlet step (Groot–Warren, `λ = 0.65`).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_dpd_temperature" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Kinetic temperature `m Σ v² / (d (N - 1))`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_engine_box_from_fractional_d1" => "Actual native MD method with checked physical or explicitly reduced reference frames. Shapes, finite state, object identity and allocation/work limits precede native work. Cartesian vector of fractional coordinates `s`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_engine_box_from_fractional_d2" => "Actual native MD method with checked physical or explicitly reduced reference frames. Shapes, finite state, object identity and allocation/work limits precede native work. Cartesian vector of fractional coordinates `s`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_engine_box_from_fractional_d3" => "Actual native MD method with checked physical or explicitly reduced reference frames. Shapes, finite state, object identity and allocation/work limits precede native work. Cartesian vector of fractional coordinates `s`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_engine_box_height_d1" => "Actual native MD method with checked physical or explicitly reduced reference frames. Shapes, finite state, object identity and allocation/work limits precede native work. Perpendicular width of the cell along lattice direction `a` (distance between faces).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_engine_box_height_d2" => "Actual native MD method with checked physical or explicitly reduced reference frames. Shapes, finite state, object identity and allocation/work limits precede native work. Perpendicular width of the cell along lattice direction `a` (distance between faces).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_engine_box_height_d3" => "Actual native MD method with checked physical or explicitly reduced reference frames. Shapes, finite state, object identity and allocation/work limits precede native work. Perpendicular width of the cell along lattice direction `a` (distance between faces).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_engine_box_matrix_d1" => "Actual native MD method with checked physical or explicitly reduced reference frames. Shapes, finite state, object identity and allocation/work limits precede native work. Cell matrix (rows are lattice vectors; diagonal for an orthorhombic box).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_engine_box_matrix_d2" => "Actual native MD method with checked physical or explicitly reduced reference frames. Shapes, finite state, object identity and allocation/work limits precede native work. Cell matrix (rows are lattice vectors; diagonal for an orthorhombic box).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_engine_box_matrix_d3" => "Actual native MD method with checked physical or explicitly reduced reference frames. Shapes, finite state, object identity and allocation/work limits precede native work. Cell matrix (rows are lattice vectors; diagonal for an orthorhombic box).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_engine_box_min_image_d1" => "Actual native MD method with checked physical or explicitly reduced reference frames. Shapes, finite state, object identity and allocation/work limits precede native work. Applies the minimum-image convention (including Lees-Edwards offset) to a separation.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
