    "num_native_graphics_vector3_magnitude_squared" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Returns the squared magnitude (avoids sqrt).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_graphics_vector3_new" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Creates a new 3D vector.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_graphics_vector3_normalize" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Normalizes the vector to have a magnitude of 1.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_are_conjugate" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Whether `x` and `y` are conjugate in the group.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_base" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The base.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_basic_orbit_lengths" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The lengths of the basic orbits.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_center" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The centre.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_centralizer" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The centraliser of `x` in the group.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_conjugacy_classes" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The conjugacy classes as `(representative, size)`, sorted by element order and then size; `None` when random search did not complete the class equation within `max_tries` samples. Random elements and all their powers are sampled; a sample in no known class (cycle type first, then a conjugacy test) opens a class of size `|G| / |C(g)|`. The result is exact: it is returned only when the class sizes sum to the order.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_conjugating_element" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. An element `g` with `g x g⁻¹ = y`, if `x` and `y` are conjugate.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_contains" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Whether `p` belongs to the group.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_contains_group" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Whether `other` is a subgroup.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_degree" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The degree.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_derived_subgroup" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The derived subgroup `[G, G]`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_elements" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Every element (only for small groups; `None` above `limit`).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_exponent" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The exponent: the lcm of the element orders (over class representatives).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_extend" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Adds a generator, keeping the chain (incremental Schreier–Sims).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_generators" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The generators the group was built from.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_intersection" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The intersection with another group of the same degree.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_is_abelian" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Whether every pair of generators commutes.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_is_normal" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Whether `h` is a normal subgroup.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_is_solvable" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Whether the group is solvable.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_is_transitive" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Whether the group acts transitively.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_new" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The group generated by `gens`, all of degree `n`. Generators of another degree are ignored; an empty list gives the trivial group.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_normal_closure" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The normal closure of `x`'s group in this group.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_normalizer" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The normaliser of the subgroup `h` (generated inside this group's degree; it need not be a subgroup).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_orbits" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The orbits of the group on `0..n`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_order" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The order: the product of the basic orbit lengths.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_pointwise_stabilizer" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The pointwise stabiliser of `points`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_random_element" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. A uniformly random element.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_set_stabilizer" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The stabiliser of the set `points`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_solvable_composition_factors" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The composition factors of a solvable group, as the primes `p` of the cyclic factors `C_p` (with multiplicity, top of the series first); `None` for a non-solvable group.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_strong_generators" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. A strong generating set (the union of the level generators).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_subgroup" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The subgroup `{g ∈ G : property(g)}`, which must be a subgroup. `prune(level, point, image)` may reject a partial element as soon as it maps the base point `point` to `image`: return `false` when no element of the subgroup can do that. Pruning must never reject a subgroup element; it only makes the search faster.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_group_sylow_subgroup" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. A Sylow `p`-subgroup. Grows a `p`-subgroup `P` by `p`-elements of its normaliser outside it until `|P|` is the full power of `p` dividing `|G|` (a `p`-subgroup is Sylow exactly when `p` does not divide `[N(P) : P]`, so a `p`-element of `N(P) \\\\ P` exists until then). `None` if random sampling failed `max_tries` times in a row.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_trivial" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The trivial group of degree `n`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_group_with_base_prefix" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The same group with a chain whose base starts with `prefix`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_hessian_diagonal_scaled" => "Evaluate the diagonal of the Hessian of a scalar callback at a measured point, returning one value per coordinate in output units divided by squared coordinate units. The common arguments are point, positive coordinate reference, positive output reference and evaluation budget. The with_steps variant takes a positive step per coordinate, in coordinate units, before the callback. Computes the second partial derivatives along the coordinate axes. Uses one central evaluation and two evaluations per axis on an interior stencil. At a finite floating-point boundary it uses three inward samples. An empty point yields an empty diagonal.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_hessian_diagonal_with_steps_scaled" => "Evaluate the diagonal of the Hessian of a scalar callback at a measured point, returning one value per coordinate in output units divided by squared coordinate units. The common arguments are point, positive coordinate reference, positive output reference and evaluation budget. The with_steps variant takes a positive step per coordinate, in coordinate units, before the callback. Computes the Hessian diagonal with a separate nominal step for each axis. If a step would leave a coordinate unchanged, it uses the adjacent representable coordinate and the actual distance in the difference. # Errors Returns [`NumericError::ShapeMismatch`] for a mismatched step count and [`NumericError::Domain`] for nonfinite coordinates or unusable steps.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_hessian_scaled" => "Native finite-difference calculus with physical reference scales: point,coordinate_scale,value_scale,max_evaluations,[partial index or Jacobian output count],callback. Independent D/E units; derivative E/D, Hessian/Laplacian E/D^2. References are positive. Shared callback errors and finite evaluation budgets are preserved. Hessian of `f` at `point`, in row-major order. Uses central differences, with an inward stencil for diagonal entries at a finite floating-point boundary. The result is symmetric.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_homology_induced_chain_map" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The matrix (over `L`'s `k`-simplices, columns `K`'s) of the chain map induced by a simplicial map.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_homology_induced_homology" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The matrix of `f_*: H_k(K; Q) -> H_k(L; Q)` in the homology bases chosen by this module (rows: `L`, columns: `K`).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_homology_is_simplicial_map" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Whether the vertex map sends every simplex of `k` onto a simplex of `l`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_homotopy_certify_endpoints" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Certifies the finite regular endpoints of a homotopy run against the original `system` (Smale's alpha test plus pairwise ball disjointness).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_homotopy_certify_endpoints_rigorous" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Certifies the finite endpoints of a homotopy run rigorously. Endpoints at infinity, ill-conditioned endpoints and the centroids of clusters of close roots are reported as uncertified; a certified endpoint is a proved simple zero.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_homotopy_certify_homotopy_node" => "Native rigorous homotopy node in explicitly normalized homogeneous projective coordinates. Patch coefficients, gamma and complex continuation time are dimensionless; this proof object retains dimensionless projective coordinates. Certifies one node of a homotopy path: proves that `H(·, t)` has exactly one zero in a small box around the homogeneous point `x`. `homogenised` and `degrees` are the data of [`crate::kernels::homotopy::homotopy_solve`]'s problem; `x` has `n + 1` entries. Used by the tracker when [`crate::kernels::homotopy::HomotopyOptions::certify_steps`] is set.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_homotopy_certify_zero" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Certifies a simple zero of a real-coefficient system near `guess`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_homotopy_certify_zero_terms" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Certifies a simple zero near `guess`, trying a ladder of box sizes. Returns `None` when no box in the ladder passes the Krawczyk test (a multiple zero, a singular Jacobian, or an endpoint that is not accurate enough to inflate a certified box around).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_homotopy_disjoint" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Whether two certified boxes are disjoint (some component separates them, which proves that they cannot contain a common point).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_homotopy_ends_data" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_homotopy_homotopy_solve_certified" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Runs [`homotopy_solve`] and certifies the endpoints. Certification is [`certify_endpoints`]. If the run is in plain `f64` and not every path ends in a certified, distinct zero, the whole solve is repeated with [`crate::kernels::homotopy::Precision::Adaptive`] and the more complete result is returned. # Errors As [`homotopy_solve`].\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_homotopy_homotopy_solve_verified" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Runs [`homotopy_solve`] and certifies the endpoints rigorously. Tracking steps are certified as well ([`HomotopyOptions::certify_steps`] is turned on for the run, which the double-precision arithmetic supports). Runs with [`Precision::Double`] escalate to [`Precision::Adaptive`] when the rigorous report is incomplete and the escalated run certifies more distinct zeros. # Errors As [`homotopy_solve`].\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_homotopy_node_terms" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The homogenised system `H(X, t) = 0` of the total-degree homotopy at a complex `t`, as complex-coefficient terms in the `n + 1` homogeneous variables. `H_i = γ (1 - t)(X_{i+1}^{d_i} - X_0^{d_i}) + t f_i(X)` for `i = 0..n`, plus the patch equation `-1 + Σ_k a_k X_k` (the same rows as [`crate::kernels::homotopy`] evaluates). `None` for a malformed system.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_homotopy_smale_alpha" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Smale's `beta`, `gamma` and `alpha` for the square polynomial system `system` at the point `x` (one complex number per variable). Returns `None` for malformed inputs, a singular Jacobian, or norms that cannot be computed within the numerical range.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_homotopy_solve" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Solves a square polynomial system by total-degree homotopy continuation. Solves the square polynomial system `system[i] = 0` (terms of equation `i`, exponent vectors with one entry per variable) by total-degree homotopy continuation in projective coordinates with a Cauchy endgame and path-jumping protection; see the module documentation. One [`PathEnd`] is returned per start solution (the product of the degrees). Regular finite endpoints are Newton-polished; singular finite endpoints and endpoints at infinity are classified with their winding number. [`HomotopyOptions::precision`] selects double, double-double or adaptive extended-precision tracking. # Errors [`RootError::Invalid`] for an empty system, exponent vectors of the wrong length, nonfinite coefficients, equations without a positive declared degree, or a product of equation degrees above 100 000.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_homotopy_verify_zero" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Verifies a zero of a real-coefficient system near `guess`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_homotopy_verify_zero_terms" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Verifies a zero near `guess` inside the box of relative half-width `relative` (a complex-coefficient system). Returns the contracted enclosure when the Krawczyk test proves that the box contains exactly one zero; `None` is inconclusive.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_hyperdual_first" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased. The coefficient of `ε₁` (the first derivative along direction one).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_hyperdual_mixed" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased. The coefficient of `ε₁ε₂` (the mixed second derivative).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_hyperdual_new" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased. `a + b ε₁ + c ε₂ + d ε₁ε₂`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_hyperdual_second" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased. The coefficient of `ε₂` (the first derivative along direction two).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_hyperdual_value" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased. The value `a`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_interval_bounds" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_interval_contains" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased. Whether `x` lies in the interval.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_interval_is_point" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased. Whether the interval is a single point.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_interval_new" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_interval_point" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased. The degenerate interval `[x, x]`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_intrinsic_apply" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased. The function on `f64`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_intrinsic_derivative" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased. The derivative on `f64`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_intrinsic_second_derivative" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased. The second derivative on `f64`. These are the classical formulas. `abs`, `floor` and `ceil` report zero everywhere, including at their kinks, where the derivative does not exist.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_irfft_plan_apply" => "Transform a finite rank-one half spectrum with n/2 + 1 bins, or zero bins for n = 0. Imaginary DC and even Nyquist components do not contribute. Returns n real 1/n-normalized samples as a measured tensor with the spectrum's physical units. In Rust, IrfftPlan::apply_into writes into a caller-owned output slice. Writes one inverse real FFT to the supplied sample slice. # Errors Returns [`IrfftError::Shape`] and leaves the output untouched unless both slices match the plan.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_irfft_plan_new" => "Prepare a fixed-length inverse real FFT for repeated half spectra in this session. Supply the number of real output samples, from 0 through 262143. This determines odd or even transform parity and the required bin count. The plan holds the even-length unpacking factors. Prepares an inverse transform whose output has `n` real samples. # Errors Returns [`IrfftError::Length`] if the output or FFT workspace size exceeds the maximum size of a slice.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_irfft_plan_output_len" => "Report the number of real samples produced by this session's inverse real FFT plan. Real sample count of the inverse transform.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_irfft_plan_spectrum_len" => "Report the number of half-spectrum bins required by this session's inverse real FFT plan. The empty plan requires zero bins. Number of nonredundant bins, or zero for an empty transform.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_ising_measure_seeded" => "Measure a seeded periodic two-dimensional Ising lattice after thermalization, then sample after each positive stride within the requested sweeps. A physical frame accepts temperature in kelvin and converts it using Boltzmann's constant. Return final row-major spins, sample count and per-site observables. Energy uses the frame's energy units, susceptibility uses inverse energy and heat capacity is reported over Boltzmann's constant. Binder is None when all measured magnetizations are zero. Sweeps and measurements count toward the site-work budget. Measures a seeded periodic 2D checkerboard Ising run after thermalization. Discards `thermalisation` sweeps, then runs `params.mc_steps` more. Measures after every `sample_every` sweeps in the latter interval and returns the final spins alongside the per-site averages. Incomplete sampling intervals still advance the spins. Measurements use constant extra storage and do not consume random draws. The bond energy counts the right and lower bond of every spin. Unit axes therefore contribute a constant self-bond energy, and extent-two axes have two bonds between the same pair. Susceptibility uses the variance of absolute magnetization. Binder is NaN when all measured magnetizations vanish. # Errors Returns an error for an invalid lattice, an overflowing sweep total, no complete measurement interval, or a nonpositive temperature or nonfinite inverse temperature.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_ising_phase_transition_scenario" => "IO: execute the original native hard-coded phase-transition scenario, create its caller-selected output directory and write CSV/NPY files. Explicit work acknowledgement requires205million site updates. Coordinates/temperature are the original reduced-unit demonstration; no physical values are silently erased. An example scenario that simulates the Ising model across a range of temperatures to observe the phase transition. # Errors This function will return an error if it fails to reshape the `Array2<f64>` for NPY output or if it fails to create or write to the output files (CSV or NPY). The files `ising_low_temp_state.npy`, `ising_high_temp_state.npy` and `ising_magnetization_vs_temp.csv` are written into `output_dir`, which is created if missing.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_ising_run_ising_simulation" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Runs an Ising model simulation with the fixed seed [`DEFAULT_ISING_SEED`]. Equivalent to [`run_ising_simulation_seeded`]; repeated calls with the same parameters return identical results.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_ising_run_ising_simulation_seeded" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Runs an Ising model simulation whose random numbers all derive from `seed`. The initial configuration and every row update use their own generator derived from `seed`, so the result does not depend on thread scheduling. Grids with an axis of length one or two use ordered single-site sweeps. At positive temperature on a multi-site grid, each visit in such a sweep proposes a flip with probability one half.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_ising_run_lattice_simulation_d1" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Monte Carlo of a spin model on a hypercubic lattice of any dimension. Ising, Potts, XY or Heisenberg on a lattice of **any** dimension `D` (periodic or open), delegating to [`crate::sim::spin_models`]. Returns the per-site averages over `sweeps` measurements after `thermalisation` updates. # Errors Fails for invalid lattices, `temperature <= 0` or unsupported model/algorithm combinations (for example cluster updates with a field).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_ising_run_lattice_simulation_d2" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Monte Carlo of a spin model on a hypercubic lattice of any dimension. Ising, Potts, XY or Heisenberg on a lattice of **any** dimension `D` (periodic or open), delegating to [`crate::sim::spin_models`]. Returns the per-site averages over `sweeps` measurements after `thermalisation` updates. # Errors Fails for invalid lattices, `temperature <= 0` or unsupported model/algorithm combinations (for example cluster updates with a field).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_ising_run_lattice_simulation_d3" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Monte Carlo of a spin model on a hypercubic lattice of any dimension. Ising, Potts, XY or Heisenberg on a lattice of **any** dimension `D` (periodic or open), delegating to [`crate::sim::spin_models`]. Returns the per-site averages over `sweeps` measurements after `thermalisation` updates. # Errors Fails for invalid lattices, `temperature <= 0` or unsupported model/algorithm combinations (for example cluster updates with a field).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_ising_run_wolff_simulation" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The Wolff single-cluster algorithm: a cluster grown from a random seed spin, each aligned neighbour added with probability `1 - exp(-2/T)`, is flipped as a whole. Rejection-free and free of critical slowing down, so it samples near `T_c` far better than local Metropolis updates. `sweeps` cluster updates are measured after `thermalisation` discarded ones. Runs on the dimension-generic engine [`crate::sim::spin_models::OnModel`] (cold start, periodic `width x height` lattice); the observables are `NaN` for lattices the engine rejects (periodic sides below 3).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_jacobian_scaled" => "Native finite-difference calculus with physical reference scales: point,coordinate_scale,value_scale,max_evaluations,[partial index or Jacobian output count],callback. Independent D/E units; derivative E/D, Hessian/Laplacian E/D^2. References are positive. Shared callback errors and finite evaluation budgets are preserved. Jacobian of `f: R^n -> R^m` at `point`, in row-major order (`m` rows of `n` entries). `f` writes its `m` outputs into its second argument.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_jit_backend_cache_key" => "Actual feature-gated native JIT adapter. Requires RSSN jit; disabled builds return Unsupported. Compiled expression calls retain physical tape frames; low-level LIR has explicit normalized values and bounded acyclic control flow. A cache fingerprint of `tape` under this backend's context. Internal lookup also checks full program equality, so collisions of this fingerprint cannot alias native code.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_jit_backend_cached" => "Actual feature-gated native JIT adapter. Requires RSSN jit; disabled builds return Unsupported. Compiled expression calls retain physical tape frames; low-level LIR has explicit normalized values and bounded acyclic control flow. Number of distinct programs compiled so far.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_jit_backend_compile" => "Actual feature-gated native JIT adapter. Requires RSSN jit; disabled builds return Unsupported. Compiled expression calls retain physical tape frames; low-level LIR has explicit normalized values and bounded acyclic control flow. Compile an already-lowered tape through the exact program cache. Concurrent callers for the same tape share one compilation and code owner. Optimize the tape first when desired; this method preserves the supplied instruction order and validates it before native code emission. # Errors Returns [`BackendError::Codegen`] for an invalid tape, unsupported host, or a code-generation failure.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_jit_backend_key_extra" => "Actual feature-gated native JIT adapter. Requires RSSN jit; disabled builds return Unsupported. Compiled expression calls retain physical tape frames; low-level LIR has explicit normalized values and bounded acyclic control flow. The context key mixed into every cache key.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_jit_backend_new" => "Actual feature-gated native JIT adapter. Requires RSSN jit; disabled builds return Unsupported. Compiled expression calls retain physical tape frames; low-level LIR has explicit normalized values and bounded acyclic control flow. A backend with an empty cache and no context key.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_jit_backend_set_key" => "Actual feature-gated native JIT adapter. Requires RSSN jit; disabled builds return Unsupported. Compiled expression calls retain physical tape frames; low-level LIR has explicit normalized values and bounded acyclic control flow. Changes the context key, dropping everything compiled under the old one.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_jit_backend_with_key" => "Actual feature-gated native JIT adapter. Requires RSSN jit; disabled builds return Unsupported. Compiled expression calls retain physical tape frames; low-level LIR has explicit normalized values and bounded acyclic control flow. A backend whose cache keys are mixed with `key_extra`. Pass [`target_key`] combined with the manifest hash: `backend = CraneliftBackend::with_key(manifest.hash_u64() ^ target_key())`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_jit_compile" => "Actual feature-gated native JIT adapter. Requires RSSN jit; disabled builds return Unsupported. Compiled expression calls retain physical tape frames; low-level LIR has explicit normalized values and bounded acyclic control flow. Compiles `tape` (which should already be optimised). # Errors [`BackendError::Codegen`] when Cranelift rejects the program or the host is unsupported, or the tape fails structural/arity validation.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_jit_eval" => "Actual feature-gated native JIT adapter. Requires RSSN jit; disabled builds return Unsupported. Compiled expression calls retain physical tape frames; low-level LIR has explicit normalized values and bounded acyclic control flow.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_jit_is_compiled" => "Actual feature-gated native JIT adapter. Requires RSSN jit; disabled builds return Unsupported. Compiled expression calls retain physical tape frames; low-level LIR has explicit normalized values and bounded acyclic control flow. Whether a tiered function returned by [`TieredBackend`] has switched to machine code (for diagnostics and tests).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_jit_lir_call" => "Actual feature-gated native JIT adapter. Requires RSSN jit; disabled builds return Unsupported. Compiled expression calls retain physical tape frames; low-level LIR has explicit normalized values and bounded acyclic control flow. Calls `func` with `args` in machine code. # Errors The arguments do not match the function (see [`Module::check_args`]).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_jit_lir_compile" => "Actual feature-gated native JIT adapter. Requires RSSN jit; disabled builds return Unsupported. Compiled expression calls retain physical tape frames; low-level LIR has explicit normalized values and bounded acyclic control flow. Verifies and compiles every function of `module`. # Errors The module does not verify, or Cranelift rejects it.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_jit_lir_module" => "Actual feature-gated native JIT adapter. Requires RSSN jit; disabled builds return Unsupported. Compiled expression calls retain physical tape frames; low-level LIR has explicit normalized values and bounded acyclic control flow. The module this was compiled from.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_jit_tail_compile" => "Actual feature-gated native JIT adapter. Requires RSSN jit; disabled builds return Unsupported. Compiled expression calls retain physical tape frames; low-level LIR has explicit normalized values and bounded acyclic control flow. Compile a pure, well-formed multi-output scalar step to native control flow. # Errors Returns a code-generation error for invalid or unsupported tapes or hosts that cannot generate machine code.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_jit_tail_run" => "Actual feature-gated native JIT adapter. Requires RSSN jit; disabled builds return Unsupported. Compiled expression calls retain physical tape frames; low-level LIR has explicit normalized values and bounded acyclic control flow. Run until a result or until the next jump would exceed `fuel`. Returns `None` for a mismatched input count.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_jit_target_key" => "Actual feature-gated native JIT adapter. Requires RSSN jit; disabled builds return Unsupported. Compiled expression calls retain physical tape frames; low-level LIR has explicit normalized values and bounded acyclic control flow. A stable identifier for the machine this code will run on. The value is a hash of the target triple and the CPU feature set the compiler was configured with, so two builds for different micro- architectures do not share cached machine code.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_kernels_sparse_exact_is_prime_u64" => "Deterministic Miller-Rabin for 64-bit integers.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_laplacian_scaled" => "Native finite-difference calculus with physical reference scales: point,coordinate_scale,value_scale,max_evaluations,[partial index or Jacobian output count],callback. Independent D/E units; derivative E/D, Hessian/Laplacian E/D^2. References are positive. Shared callback errors and finite evaluation budgets are preserved. Laplacian of a scalar field, using only the diagonal Hessian stencil.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_levin_t" => "Physical native series/sequence convergence. sum_series: start,max_terms,tolerance,value_scale,max_evaluations,term(Float)->E. sequence_limit omits start. Levin: max_terms,value_scale,max_evaluations,term(Int)->E; result includes native error estimate. References/tolerances are positive physical E; callback failures propagate and budgets bound actual host calls. Sums `term(0) + term(1) + ...` with a Levin transformation of the first `n_terms` partial sums. Returns `(estimate, error_estimate)` where the error estimate is the difference of the two highest-order transforms; the best (smallest successive difference) transform is reported. Prefer [`levin_sum_lazy`] when the terms are available directly, since this path differences the partial sums to recover them. # Errors Returns an error if fewer than four terms are requested or no finite transform could be formed.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_levin_u" => "Physical native series/sequence convergence. sum_series: start,max_terms,tolerance,value_scale,max_evaluations,term(Float)->E. sequence_limit omits start. Levin: max_terms,value_scale,max_evaluations,term(Int)->E; result includes native error estimate. References/tolerances are positive physical E; callback failures propagate and budgets bound actual host calls. Sums `term(0) + term(1) + ...` with a Levin transformation of the first `n_terms` partial sums. Returns `(estimate, error_estimate)` where the error estimate is the difference of the two highest-order transforms; the best (smallest successive difference) transform is reported. Prefer [`levin_sum_lazy`] when the terms are available directly, since this path differences the partial sums to recover them. # Errors Returns an error if fewer than four terms are requested or no finite transform could be formed.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_levin_v" => "Physical native series/sequence convergence. sum_series: start,max_terms,tolerance,value_scale,max_evaluations,term(Float)->E. sequence_limit omits start. Levin: max_terms,value_scale,max_evaluations,term(Int)->E; result includes native error estimate. References/tolerances are positive physical E; callback failures propagate and budgets bound actual host calls. Sums `term(0) + term(1) + ...` with a Levin transformation of the first `n_terms` partial sums. Returns `(estimate, error_estimate)` where the error estimate is the difference of the two highest-order transforms; the best (smallest successive difference) transform is reported. Prefer [`levin_sum_lazy`] when the terms are available directly, since this path differences the partial sums to recover them. # Errors Returns an error if fewer than four terms are requested or no finite transform could be formed.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_lie_ad" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The matrix of `ad x`: column `j` holds the coordinates of `[x, e_j]`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_bracket" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. `[x, y]` in coordinates.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_bracket_spaces" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The span of all `[a_i, b_j]` (echelon basis).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_cartan_matrix" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The Cartan matrix of type `letter` and rank `n`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_cartan_solvable_test" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Cartan's first criterion: `g` is solvable iff `K(g, [g, g]) = 0`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_cartan_subalgebra" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. A Cartan subalgebra: the generalised zero eigenspace of a regular element, chosen among dense and sparse pseudo-random candidates for the smallest dimension and then for the most rational roots (sparse candidates find the split tori of matrix algebras with a diagonal part).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_casimir" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The quadratic Casimir operator `sum K^{ab} rho(e_a) rho(e_b)` of a representation `rho` (one matrix per basis element) for the Killing form; the algebra must be semisimple.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_center" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The center.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_charpoly" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The characteristic polynomial `det(x I - m)` as coefficients of `x^0 ..= x^n` (Faddeev-LeVerrier).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_components" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The connected components (as index lists) of the Dynkin diagram.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_derived_series" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The derived series `g ⊇ [g, g] ⊇ ...` up to the point it stabilises.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_euclidean_simple_roots" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The standard simple roots of a type in Euclidean coordinates. Those of Bourbaki, not normalised to a common length: `A_n` lives in `R^{n+1}`, the exceptional `E`-types in `R^8`, `F_4` in `R^4`, `G_2` in `R^3`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_from_constants" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. A Lie algebra from structure constants; `None` unless the bracket is antisymmetric and satisfies the Jacobi identity.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_from_matrices" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The Lie algebra spanned by a basis of rational matrices. Returns `None` unless the basis is nonempty, consists of square matrices of the same positive order, and is independent and closed under the commutator. The structure constants use the input basis order.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_is_nilpotent" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Whether the lower central series reaches zero.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_is_semisimple" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Cartan's second criterion: `g` is semisimple iff `K` is nondegenerate.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_is_solvable" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Whether the derived series reaches zero.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_is_subalgebra" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Whether the span of `vectors` is closed under the bracket.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_killing" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The Killing form `K_ab = tr(ad e_a ad e_b)`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_levi" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. A Levi decomposition `g = s ⋉ r`: a semisimple subalgebra `s` complementary to the radical `r` (returned as `(s, r)`), lifted through the derived series of `r` (Whitehead's lemma makes each lift a linear problem).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_lower_central_series" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The lower central series `g ⊇ [g, g] ⊇ [g, [g, g]] ⊇ ...`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_parse_type" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Parses a type name such as `A2`, `E8`, `G2`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_positive_roots" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The positive roots of the root system with Cartan matrix `a`, in simple-root coordinates, ordered by height (the root strings through the simple roots are followed level by level).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_radical" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The radical (largest solvable ideal) `= [g, g]^⊥` for the Killing form.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_rational_roots" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The distinct rational roots of the polynomial with coefficients `p[0] ..= p[n]` (rational root theorem); `None` if the coefficients are too large to factor.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_recognize" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The simple factors of the algebra with Cartan matrix `a` as `(letter, rank)` pairs, or `None` if `a` is not the Cartan matrix of a semisimple Lie algebra.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_root_decomposition" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The decomposition of `g` into simultaneous generalised eigenspaces of `ad h` for the abelian subalgebra spanned by `h`. Only roots with rational values are found; the second component counts the dimensions that belong to other (irrational or complex) roots.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_standard_basis" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The standard basis of a classical matrix Lie algebra. Matrices of Gaussian integers (`gl`, `sl`: elementary matrices and the Chevalley `H_k = E_kk - E_{k+1,k+1}`; `so(n)`: `E_ij - E_ji`; `sp(2n)`: `[[A, B], [C, -A^T]]` with `B`, `C` symmetric; `su(n)`: `E_ij - E_ji`, `i (E_ij + E_ji)`, `i H_k`).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lie_upper_central_series" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The upper central series `0 ⊆ Z_1 ⊆ Z_2 ⊆ ...` (without the leading 0).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_assign" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Emits `inst` assigning an existing register.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_bail" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Ends the current block with a bail.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_batch_from_tape" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Lowers a tape to a *batch* function that evaluates it at every row. The function's parameters are the input columns (`inputs` slices), the parameter vector (one slice), the output columns (`outputs` slices) and the row count (`I64`): for `row < rows` it stores output `k` of `row` into `out_k[row]`. Missing input elements read NaN, exactly like [`Compiled::call_batch`](super::Compiled::call_batch). Constants and parameters are loop-invariant and evaluated once before the loop. Every row gets the bits [`Tape::eval`](super::tape::Tape::eval) gives it: each tape instruction maps to the LIR instruction with the same IEEE semantics. Returns `None` for tapes with `Gather` (its column is chosen per row, which a column-per-parameter signature cannot express).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_block_param" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Adds a parameter of type `ty` to `block`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_branch" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Ends the current block with a conditional branch.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_builder_new" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. A function with the given parameter and result types; the builder is positioned in the entry block.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_check_args" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Checks host arguments against a function's parameters. # Errors Unknown function, wrong arity or types, or a read-only slice for a function that writes, or a function returning a slice.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_current" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. The block being emitted into.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_f64_to_i64" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. `x` truncated toward zero to an integer, or `None` for NaN and values outside the `i64` range (the bail condition of [`Inst::FToI`]).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_fcmp" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. The comparison of two floats.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_finish" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. The finished function. # Errors A block without a terminator.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_fmax" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. The float maximum with NaN propagation.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_fmin" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. The float minimum with NaN propagation (both executors agree on it).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_function_verify" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Checks types, arities and references. # Errors The first problem found.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_icmp" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. The comparison of two integers.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_ins" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Emits `inst` into a fresh register of its natural type and returns it. For [`Inst::Call`] and [`Inst::Copy`], whose type is not determined by the instruction alone, use [`FunctionBuilder::ins_typed`].\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_ins_typed" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Emits `inst` into a fresh register of type `ty`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_instruction" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_interpret" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Runs `func` in the reference interpreter with at most `max_steps` instructions (a runaway loop bails with [`BAIL_STEPS`]). # Errors The module does not verify, or the arguments do not match the function's parameters, or a read-only slice is passed to a function that writes.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_is_terminated" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Whether the current block already has its terminator.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_jump" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Ends the current block with a jump.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_module" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_module_verify" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Checks types, arities and references. # Errors The first problem found.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_new_block" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. A new, empty block.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_outcome" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Runs `func` in the reference interpreter with at most `max_steps` instructions (a runaway loop bails with [`BAIL_STEPS`]). # Errors The module does not verify, or the arguments do not match the function's parameters, or a read-only slice is passed to a function that writes.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_outcome_values" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. The returned values, if the call did not bail.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_param" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Parameter `i` of the function.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_reg" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. A fresh register of type `ty`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_ret" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Ends the current block with a return.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_switch_to" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Continues emitting into `block`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_ty" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. The type of a register.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_value_ty" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. The LIR type of the value.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_lir_written_params" => "Typed native LIR adapter. Machine instructions use explicit normalized IEEE values, checked register/block/type references and bounded native interpreter steps. Which parameters of `func` may be stored into, by `func` itself or by anything it calls: a slice argument passed for such a parameter must be writable, every other one may be read-only. Slices cannot be created in LIR, only passed along, so the analysis follows each slice register back to the parameters it may alias (through copies, block parameters and call arguments) and iterates over the whole module to a fixpoint (calls may recurse).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_apply_pbc" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Applies periodic boundary conditions to a position.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_berendsen_thermostat" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Berendsen thermostat. Gently couples the system to a heat bath. # Arguments * `particles` - System particles * `target_temp` - Target temperature * `tau` - Coupling time constant * `dt` - Time step\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_center_of_mass" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Calculates the center of mass of the system. # Errors Returns an error if the particle list is empty.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_cloud" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_cloud_data" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_coulomb_interaction" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Coulomb (electrostatic) potential. V(r) = `k_e` * q1 * q2 / r # Arguments * `p1`, `p2` - The two particles (with charge fields) * `k_coulomb` - Coulomb constant (in appropriate units) # Errors Returns an error if the particles have different dimensions.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_create_cubic_lattice" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Creates a simple cubic lattice of particles.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_create_fcc_lattice" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Creates an FCC (face-centered cubic) lattice of particles.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_frame" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_gaussian_stream_new" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. A stream seeded with `seed`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_gaussian_stream_next" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. A standard normal deviate.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_harmonic_interaction" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Harmonic (spring) potential. V(r) = 0.5 * k * (r - r0)² # Arguments * `p1`, `p2` - The two particles * `k` - Spring constant * `r0` - Equilibrium distance # Errors Returns an error if the particles have different dimensions.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_initialize_velocities_maxwell_boltzmann" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Initializes particle velocities from Maxwell-Boltzmann distribution.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_integrate_langevin_baoab" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Langevin dynamics with the BAOAB splitting (Leimkuhler–Matthews): half kick (B), half drift (A), exact Ornstein–Uhlenbeck velocity update with friction `gamma` at temperature `kt` (O), half drift, half kick. Samples the canonical ensemble with configurational error `O(dt²)`. # Errors Propagates errors of the force calculation.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_md_integrate_nose_hoover" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. The Nosé–Hoover thermostat: the friction `ξ` obeys `Q dξ/dt = Σ m v² - N_f kT`, a deterministic extended system whose invariant `H + Q ξ²/2 + N_f kT s` (with `ds/dt = ξ`) is conserved. Velocity-Verlet with the friction applied as an exact exponential scaling in half steps. Returns the final `(ξ, s)`. # Errors Propagates errors of the force calculation.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_md_integrate_velocity_verlet" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Integrates the equations of motion for a system of particles using the Velocity Verlet algorithm. The Velocity Verlet algorithm is a popular numerical integration scheme for molecular dynamics simulations. It is time-reversible and preserves phase space volume, making it suitable for long-term simulations. # Arguments * `particles` - A mutable vector of `Particle`s. * `dt` - The time step. * `num_steps` - The number of simulation steps. * `force_calculator` - A closure that computes the total force on each particle. It takes `&mut Vec<Particle>` and returns `Result<(), String>`. # Returns A `Vec<Vec<Particle>>` representing the trajectory of the particles over time. # Errors Returns an error if the force calculator fails or if vector operations fail due to dimension mismatch.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_md_lennard_jones_interaction" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Computes the Lennard-Jones potential and force between two particles. The Lennard-Jones potential is a simple mathematical model that describes the interaction between a pair of neutral atoms or molecules. It has a repulsive term at short distances and an attractive term at long distances. # Arguments * `p1`, `p2` - The two particles. * `epsilon` - The depth of the potential well. * `sigma` - The finite distance at which the inter-particle potential is zero. # Returns A tuple `(potential, force_on_p1)` where `potential` is the scalar potential energy and `force_on_p1` is the force vector acting on `p1` due to `p2`. # Errors Returns an error if the particles have different dimensions.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_mean_square_displacement" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Calculates mean square displacement. MSD(t) = <|r(t) - r(0)|²>\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_minimum_image_distance" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Applies minimum image convention for distance calculation.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_morse_interaction" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Morse potential for diatomic molecules. V(r) = De * (1 - exp(-a(r - re)))² # Arguments * `p1`, `p2` - The two particles * `de` - Dissociation energy * `a` - Controls the width of the potential well * `re` - Equilibrium bond distance Separations below `1e-9` return infinite energy and a zero force vector. [`morse_radial`] evaluates the scalar curve at all nonnegative distances. # Errors Returns an error if the particles have different dimensions.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_morse_radial" => "Evaluate the Morse energy and signed radial force in a checked reference frame. Energy is zero at the equilibrium distance. Positive force points toward increasing separation. A zero separation returns the one-sided radial force. Returns the Morse energy and the force along increasing distance. The minimum is zero at `r = re`. At `r = 0` the scalar force is the one-sided radial derivative with a negative sign. There is no direction to assign to that force at coincident particle positions. # Errors The distance, depth and equilibrium distance must be finite and nonnegative. The inverse length `a` must be finite and positive. Returns an error when the energy or radial force exceeds finite range.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_neighbour_pairs" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_normalized_frame" => "Explicit reduced-unit native frame; all numeric values are dimensionless and kB equals one.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_particle_data" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_particle_distance_to" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Distance to another particle # Errors Returns an error if the particles have different dimensions.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_particle_kinetic_energy" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Returns the kinetic energy of the particle: KE = 0.5 * m * v²\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_particle_momentum" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Returns the momentum of the particle: p = m * v\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_particle_new" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Creates a new particle with default charge and type.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_particle_speed" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Returns the speed (magnitude of velocity)\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_particle_with_charge" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Creates a new particle with charge.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_pressure" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Calculates instantaneous pressure using the virial theorem. P = (N * `k_B` * T + virial) / V\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_radial_distribution_function" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Calculates the radial distribution function g(r). # Arguments * `particles` - System particles * `box_size` - Box dimensions * `num_bins` - Number of histogram bins * `r_max` - Maximum distance to consider # Returns (`r_values`, `g_r`) where `r_values` are bin centers and `g_r` are g(r) values\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_remove_com_velocity" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Removes center of mass velocity from the system. # Errors Returns an error if the particle list is empty.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_run_engine_md" => "Run the real native MD engine. Physical thermal targets are Kelvin in SI frames and reduced kBT in normalized frames; LJ energy/length, time, box, count and work bounds are validated. Runs Lennard-Jones MD for a runtime dimension on the const-generic engine. Parameters `(epsilon, sigma, r_cut)` give a shifted-force potential in a periodic box on the const-generic engine ([`crate::sim::md_engine::MdSimulation`]) for a **runtime** dimension of 1, 2 or 3, and writes positions, velocities and forces back into `particles`. Returns the final total energy. # Errors Fails for dimensions other than 1-3, mismatching vector lengths or engine errors.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_soft_sphere_interaction" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Soft-sphere potential for avoiding particle overlap. V(r) = ε * (σ/r)^n for r < σ, 0 otherwise # Errors Returns an error if the particles have different dimensions.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_temperature" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Calculates the temperature from kinetic energy. T = 2 * KE / (dim * N * `k_B`) In reduced units with `k_B` = 1: T = 2 * KE / (dim * N)\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_total_kinetic_energy" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Calculates the total kinetic energy of the system.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_total_momentum" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Calculates the total momentum of the system. # Errors Returns an error if the particle list is empty.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_md_velocity_rescale" => "Physical particle adapter. Coordinates, velocity, mass, charge, force, energy and thermal targets use checked reference units; count, shape and work bounds precede native work. Velocity rescaling thermostat. Rescales velocities to achieve target temperature.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_mm_compute_density_and_forces" => "Recompute density, pressure and forces at the current positions of a reduced-unit legacy SPH system. Call the integration operator separately to advance the particles. Updates density, pressure and force for the current positions and velocities. Reuses one neighborhood search for both interaction sweeps.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_mm_compute_density_pressure" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Computes the density and pressure of each particle.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_mm_compute_forces" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Computes the forces acting on each particle.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_mm_dam_break_scenario" => "Execute the original hard-coded native demonstration in its explicitly normalized model coordinates. No physical-unit interpretation is inferred. Simulates a 2D dam break scenario using Smoothed-Particle Hydrodynamics (SPH). This function initializes a block of fluid particles (the \"dam\") and simulates its collapse and flow under gravity. It demonstrates the SPH method's ability to model fluid dynamics without a fixed mesh. # Returns A `Vec` of tuples `(x, y)` representing the final positions of the particles.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_mm_integrate" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Integrates the equations of motion for each particle.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_mm_poly6_new" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Creates a new Poly6 kernel.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_mm_spiky_new" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Creates a new spiky kernel.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_mm_state" => "Read particle positions, velocities, forces, density and pressure from the legacy SPH system in reduced units. Rows follow the original particle order. The vector fields have shape [particles,2].\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_mm_system_new" => "Legacy native educational SPH uses explicitly normalized unit-mass coefficients and3D smoothing kernels on2D sites. This adapter rejects physical quantities rather than assigning inconsistent SI force dimensions; use the general Sph<D> adapters for coherent physical models.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_mm_update" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Updates the SPH system by one time step.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_mm_vector_new" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Creates a new 2D vector.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_mtm_simulate_1d_poisson_multigrid_scenario" => "Execute the original native analytic multigrid demonstration in normalized coordinates; explicit positive domain/solution references give a physical realization without reinterpreting its hard-coded coefficients. Solves a 1D Poisson problem with a known analytical solution. `-u_xx = 2` on `[0, 1]` with `u(0)=u(1)=0`. Exact solution is `u(x) = x(1-x)`. # Errors This function will return an error if the underlying `solve_poisson_1d_multigrid` function encounters an error, e.g., if the grid size is invalid.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_mtm_simulate_2d_poisson_multigrid_scenario" => "Execute the original native analytic multigrid demonstration in normalized coordinates; explicit positive domain/solution references give a physical realization without reinterpreting its hard-coded coefficients. Solves a 2D Poisson problem with a known analytical solution. # Errors This function will return an error if the underlying `solve_poisson_2d_multigrid` function encounters an error, e.g., if the grid size is invalid.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_mtm_solve_poisson_1d_multigrid" => "Actual native zero-Dirichlet multigrid on its unit interval/cube, mapped to an explicit physical coordinate and solution reference. RHS has solution/coordinate^2 units.1D input contains interior values;2D/3D input includes boundary nodes. Output is flattened in native x-fastest order with explicit shape. Solves the 1D Poisson equation `-u_xx = f` using the multigrid method. # Arguments * `n` - Number of interior points on the finest grid. Must be `2^k - 1`. * `f` - The right-hand side function values on the finest grid. * `num_cycles` - The number of V-cycles to perform. # Returns The solution vector `u`. # Errors This function will return an error if the grid size `n` is not of the form `2^k - 1`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_mtm_solve_poisson_2d_multigrid" => "Actual native zero-Dirichlet multigrid on its unit interval/cube, mapped to an explicit physical coordinate and solution reference. RHS has solution/coordinate^2 units.1D input contains interior values;2D/3D input includes boundary nodes. Output is flattened in native x-fastest order with explicit shape. Solves `-∇²u = f` on the unit square by running `num_cycles` multigrid V-cycles. Input and output are both flattened with x varying fastest. All boundary values are fixed to zero, and source entries on those boundaries are ignored. With zero cycles, or with a boundary-only 2×2 grid, the result is all zeros. # Errors Returns an error if `n` is not of the form `2^k + 1` for a nonnegative integer `k`, or if `f` does not have exactly `n * n` entries.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_mtm_solve_poisson_3d_multigrid" => "Actual native zero-Dirichlet multigrid on its unit interval/cube, mapped to an explicit physical coordinate and solution reference. RHS has solution/coordinate^2 units.1D input contains interior values;2D/3D input includes boundary nodes. Output is flattened in native x-fastest order with explicit shape. Solves the 3D Poisson equation `-Δu = f` on the unit cube. Zero Dirichlet boundary, `n` nodes per axis including the boundary, `x` fastest, `n = 2^k + 1`) with `num_cycles` multigrid V-cycles. 3D counterpart of [`solve_poisson_2d_multigrid`]; the general 1D/2D/3D entry point with any boundary conditions is [`solve_poisson_multigrid_nd`]. # Errors This function will return an error if `n` is not of the form `2^k + 1`, if `f.len() != n^3` or if the multigrid hierarchy cannot be built.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_multilinear_grid_eval" => "Interpolate a rank-one point in axis order using an existing session-local grid. A Dynamic-element point carries each coordinate's dimension separately. A homogeneous measured point supplies one shared dimension. Every coordinate must match its axis and be inside the grid. Returns a value in the grid's stored ordinate dimension. Interpolates an in-bounds point without allocating or rescanning the grid. # Errors Returns an error if the point has the wrong dimension or any coordinate is non-finite or outside its axis.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_multilinear_grid_new" => "Create an immutable session-local rectilinear grid. Axes is an ordered rank-one tensor of measured rank-one axis tensors, with independent units and possibly different lengths. Values is a measured rank-one tensor laid out with the first axis varying fastest. Axes must contain at least two finite increasing nodes each. Shape, unit, and allocation bounds are checked at construction. Prepares a shared grid for calls to [`Self::evaluate`]. # Errors Returns an error if there are no axes, any axis has fewer than two finite strictly increasing nodes, the size overflows, or the values are non-finite or have the wrong length.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_multivariate_cov" => "Native covariance matrix retains squared coordinate units. The row-major `d × d` covariance matrix. # Errors [`DistError::Empty`], [`DistError::ShapeMismatch`], or [`DistError::Domain`] on invalid parameters.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_multivariate_dim" => "Native dimension query. The dimension `d` of the distribution.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_multivariate_log_pdf" => "Native log density relative to the constructor explicit reference measure, avoiding a logarithm of dimensioned density. The natural logarithm of the probability density at `x`. # Errors [`DistError::Empty`] if the distribution has dimension 0, [`DistError::ShapeMismatch`] if `x` or `cov` has the wrong length, [`DistError::Domain`] if `Dirichlet` parameters are non-positive, or [`DistError::NotPositiveDefinite`] if `cov` is not positive definite.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_multivariate_mean" => "Native mean vector retains coordinate units. The mean vector. # Errors [`DistError::Empty`] or [`DistError::Domain`] on invalid parameters.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_multivariate_normal_new" => "Construct a native multivariate normal from homogeneous mean units and squared covariance units. A positive reference length/scale with mean units defines the dimensionless log-density reference measure. Dimension is bounded to32.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_multivariate_pdf" => "Native density with inverse coordinate units raised to the checked distribution dimension; Dirichlet remains dimensionless. The probability density at `x`. # Errors Propagates validation errors from [`MultivariateDistribution::log_pdf`].\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_multivariate_sample" => "Native FnMut uniform-source specialization using the shared authenticated random stream; output retains coordinate units. Draw one `d`-dimensional sample using a uniform source on `[0, 1)`. # Errors Propagates domain, shape, or positive-definiteness errors.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_multivector_conjugate" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Returns the Clifford conjugate of the multivector. Conjugation combines reversal and grade involution.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_multivector_dot" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Performs the inner (dot) product.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_multivector_inv" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Returns the inverse of a general `Cl(3,0)` multivector. The product with its Clifford conjugate is central (scalar plus pseudoscalar). Components of the input must be finite. Returns `None` if the determinant is exactly zero or an inverse component overflows.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_multivector_mul_central" => "Multiplies a Cl(3,0) multivector by scalar + pseudoscalar times e123. The two factor coefficients share one physical dimension. The product coefficients have that dimension times the input coefficient dimension. Multiplies by the central factor `scalar + pseudoscalar * e123`. The `e123` blade commutes with every multivector and squares to `-1`, so this operation combines four independent pairs of coefficients.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_multivector_new" => "Construct a homogeneous-coefficient Cl(3,0) multivector; the eight basis blades are dimensionless and all coefficients share physical units. Creates a new `Multivector3D` with all components.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_multivector_norm" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Returns the norm of the multivector.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_multivector_norm_sq" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Returns the squared norm of the multivector (A * reverse(A))_s.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_multivector_reverse" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Returns the reverse of the multivector. The reverse operation reverses the order of products of basis vectors. For G3: s, v1, v2, v3 are unchanged; b12, b23, b31, pss are negated. Wait, `reverse(e_i` `e_j`) = `e_j` `e_i` = -`e_i` `e_j`. So bivectors are negated. `reverse(e_1` `e_2` `e_3`) = `e_3` `e_2` `e_1` = -`e_1` `e_2` `e_3`. So pseudoscalar is negated.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_multivector_wedge" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Performs the outer (wedge) product.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_nbody_coulomb_forces_d1" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Barnes-Hut Coulomb forces `F_i = -k q_i sum_j q_j K(x_j - x_i)` (like charges repel). # Errors Propagates tree construction errors.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_nbody_coulomb_forces_d2" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Barnes-Hut Coulomb forces `F_i = -k q_i sum_j q_j K(x_j - x_i)` (like charges repel). # Errors Propagates tree construction errors.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_nbody_coulomb_forces_d3" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Barnes-Hut Coulomb forces `F_i = -k q_i sum_j q_j K(x_j - x_i)` (like charges repel). # Errors Propagates tree construction errors.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_nbody_direct_field_d1" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Direct `O(N^2)` field of all sources at every body, excluding its own contribution. Use [`direct_field_into`] when the input lengths need to be checked or the output storage is already available. `eps` sets the Plummer softening length by its magnitude. Distinct coincident bodies with zero softening have an undefined pair contribution (`NaN`). # Panics Panics in positive dimensions if there are at least two bodies and `src` is shorter than `pos`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_nbody_direct_field_d2" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Direct `O(N^2)` field of all sources at every body, excluding its own contribution. Use [`direct_field_into`] when the input lengths need to be checked or the output storage is already available. `eps` sets the Plummer softening length by its magnitude. Distinct coincident bodies with zero softening have an undefined pair contribution (`NaN`). # Panics Panics in positive dimensions if there are at least two bodies and `src` is shorter than `pos`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_nbody_direct_field_d3" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Direct `O(N^2)` field of all sources at every body, excluding its own contribution. Use [`direct_field_into`] when the input lengths need to be checked or the output storage is already available. `eps` sets the Plummer softening length by its magnitude. Distinct coincident bodies with zero softening have an undefined pair contribution (`NaN`). # Panics Panics in positive dimensions if there are at least two bodies and `src` is shorter than `pos`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_nbody_fmm2d_field" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Field `sum_j s_j (x_j - x_i) / |x_j - x_i|^2` at every point (self excluded) by an adaptive 2-D FMM of order `p` with about `ppb` points per leaf box. # Errors Fails for empty input or length mismatch.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_nbody_fmm3d_field" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Field `sum_j s_j (x_j - x_i) / |x_j - x_i|^3` at every point (self excluded) by the adaptive 3-D FMM of order `p` with about `ppb` points per leaf box. # Errors Fails for empty input or length mismatch.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_nbody_gravity_accelerations_d1" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Barnes-Hut gravitational accelerations `a_i = G sum_j m_j K(x_j - x_i)`. # Errors Propagates tree construction errors.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_nbody_gravity_accelerations_d2" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Barnes-Hut gravitational accelerations `a_i = G sum_j m_j K(x_j - x_i)`. # Errors Propagates tree construction errors.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_nbody_gravity_accelerations_d3" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Barnes-Hut gravitational accelerations `a_i = G sum_j m_j K(x_j - x_i)`. # Errors Propagates tree construction errors.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_nbody_tree_field_d1" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Field `sum_j s_j K(x_j - x)` at `x`, skipping the body `skip` (pass `usize::MAX` for none).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_nbody_tree_field_d2" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Field `sum_j s_j K(x_j - x)` at `x`, skipping the body `skip` (pass `usize::MAX` for none).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_nbody_tree_field_d3" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Field `sum_j s_j K(x_j - x)` at `x`, skipping the body `skip` (pass `usize::MAX` for none).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_nbody_tree_new_d1" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Builds the tree for sources `src` at `pos`. # Errors Fails for `D > 3`, empty input or length mismatch.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_nbody_tree_new_d2" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Builds the tree for sources `src` at `pos`. # Errors Fails for `D > 3`, empty input or length mismatch.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_nbody_tree_new_d3" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Builds the tree for sources `src` at `pos`. # Errors Fails for `D > 3`, empty input or length mismatch.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_nelder_mead_scaled" => "Native scaled global/constrained optimization with shared actual host evaluation limit. Nelder: x,xscale,yscale,step,tol,iterations,budget,f. Differential evolution: lo,hi,xscale,yscale,population,generations,budget,seed,f. Annealing: x,xscale,yscale,step,temperature,cooling,iterations,budget,seed,f. Constrained: x,xscale,yscale,equality_scale,inequality_scale,tol,iterations,budget,f,eq,ineq. Constraints independently carry C/H units; SQP returns physical multipliers E/C and E/H, native status and second-order verdict. Second-order: x,lambda,mu,xscale,yscale,eqscale,ineqscale,budget,f,eq,ineq. No global-optimality claim; native iteration/status semantics retained. Nelder–Mead simplex method, with `step` scaling the initial coordinate offsets. Tied objective values retain their previous simplex order.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_normal_dist_cdf" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Returns the cumulative distribution function (CDF) value at `x`. # Arguments * `x` - The value at which to evaluate the CDF. # Returns The CDF value as an `f64`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_normal_dist_inverse_cdf" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Returns the quantile (inverse CDF) at probability `p`. Returns `NaN` when `p` is outside `[0, 1]`; the boundary values are the (possibly infinite) support limits rather than errors.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_normal_dist_new" => "Checked native legacy distribution. Continuous parameters and queries retain coherent physical units; inverse CDF restores sample units and PDF has inverse sample units. Creates a new `NormalDist` instance. # Errors Returns an error unless both parameters are finite and `std_dev > 0`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_normal_dist_pdf" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Returns the probability density function (PDF) value at `x`. # Arguments * `x` - The value at which to evaluate the PDF. # Returns The PDF value as an `f64`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_number_exact_binomial" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Exact binomial coefficient; impossible or negative selections yield zero.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_number_exact_factor" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Prime factorization of the magnitude of `n`, grouped in increasing order.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_number_exact_falling_factorial" => "Counts the ordered selections of k distinct members from n. Inputs and result are exact dimensionless integers. An empty valid selection has one ordering, and impossible selections return zero. The adapter bounds the number of multiplied factors. Exact number of ordered selections of `k` distinct members from `n`. An empty selection has one ordering. Negative or impossible inputs return zero.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_number_exact_gcd" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Greatest common divisor of signed magnitudes. Preserves the signed-word ABI: the sole unrepresentable result, 2^63, uses its `i64::MIN` bit representation. Use arbitrary precision for that case.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_number_exact_is_negative" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Whether an exact integer is negative.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_number_exact_is_prime" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Deterministic primality for every unsigned machine word.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_number_exact_lcm" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Nonnegative least common multiple, saturated at `i64::MAX` on overflow.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_number_exact_permutations" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Exact factorial, conventionally zero for negative inputs.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_number_exact_primes" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Prime numbers strictly below `limit`; negative limits yield an empty list.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_online_covariance_correlation" => "Dimensionless Pearson correlation matrix. Returns None for fewer than two observations or any constant column. Row-major Pearson correlation matrix, or `None` when the sample has fewer than two observations or any column has zero variance.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_online_covariance_count" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Number of observations incorporated so far.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_online_covariance_dimension" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Number of variables.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_online_covariance_mean" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The mean, or `None` if no observation has been incorporated.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_online_covariance_merge" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Merge another independent accumulator into this one. # Errors Reports a dimension mismatch, count overflow, or arithmetic overflow.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_online_covariance_new" => "Create an online accumulator for homogeneous observation units specified by a positive reference quantity. Coherent means retain those units and covariance squares them. Construct an empty accumulator for `dimension` variables. # Errors Returns [`OnlineStatsError::InvalidDimension`] for zero or an unallocatable matrix size.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_online_covariance_population_covariance" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Population covariance (divisor `n`), or `None` when empty.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_online_covariance_push" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Incorporate one observation. # Errors Reports a dimension mismatch, non-finite input, or arithmetic overflow.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_online_covariance_push_batch" => "Atomically incorporate a row-major tensor of observations with the accumulator's coordinate units. Columns must match the accumulator dimension. Incorporate a flat row-major batch atomically. Each row contains [`Self::dimension`] values. Large batches use bounded shards and combine them in row order, independent of worker count. An empty batch leaves the accumulator unchanged. # Errors Returns an error for an incomplete row, non-finite input, count or arithmetic overflow, or failure to allocate a shard.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_online_covariance_push_frequency_batch" => "Atomically incorporate a row-major tensor of observations with the accumulator's coordinate units and one nonnegative, dimensionless integer frequency per row. Each frequency counts repeated observations without expanding the tensor. Incorporate a flat row-major batch with an integer frequency per row. Each row represents as many identical observations as its frequency, with no need to expand those observations. A zero frequency adds no observations. All row values must be finite. The resulting count is the sum of frequencies and the previous count. Sample covariance divides by the resulting count minus one. Floating-point results can differ from pushing each repetition individually. Shards and their merge order are independent of worker count. # Errors An incomplete row, a frequency vector of the wrong length, a non-finite value, count or arithmetic overflow, or a shard allocation failure leaves the accumulator unchanged.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_online_covariance_sample_covariance" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Unbiased sample covariance (divisor `n - 1`), or `None` for fewer than two observations.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_ordering_amd_order" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Approximate minimum degree ordering of the pattern `adj`. Returns `perm` with `perm[new] = old` (a permutation of `0..adj.len()`). The pattern must be symmetric. Duplicate entries and self loops do not affect the ordering. # Panics A neighbour index is outside `0..adj.len()`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_ordering_cholesky_fill" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Number of nonzeros of the Cholesky factor `L` (including the diagonal) of the pattern `adj` ordered by `perm` (`perm[new] = old`), by symbolic factorisation along the elimination tree.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_ordering_metrics" => "Measures the permuted half-bandwidth and lower-triangle profile from CSR adjacency offsets and neighbour indices. The zero-based permutation maps each new position to its old vertex. Single-direction and repeated edges describe the same undirected pattern. Measures the bandwidth and profile of a permuted sparse pattern. `perm[new] = old` names the original vertex at each reordered position. Edges may be listed in either or both directions. Duplicate and diagonal entries leave both metrics unchanged. The work is linear in the number of vertices and listed edges, with linear storage in the vertex count. # Errors The permutation is malformed, a neighbour is out of range, or the accumulated profile does not fit a `usize`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_ordering_ml_hybrid_nested_dissection_order" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Best of approximate minimum degree and multilevel nested dissection. Two leaf sizes are tried and judged by the exact symbolic Cholesky fill ([`cholesky_fill`]); the result is never worse than [`amd_order`] and, on large two- and three-dimensional meshes, usually better.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_ordering_ml_multilevel_nested_dissection_order" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Multilevel nested dissection ordering of the pattern `adj` (see the module documentation). Returns `perm` with `perm[new] = old`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_ordering_ml_multilevel_nested_dissection_with" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. As [`multilevel_nested_dissection_order`] with explicit parameters.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_ordering_ml_vertex_separator_bisection" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. One multilevel vertex-separator bisection of a connected pattern: returns `(left, right, separator)`; no edge joins `left` and `right`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_ordering_nested_dissection_order" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Nested dissection ordering by recursive level-structure bisection. Pieces of at most 300 vertices are ordered by [`amd_order`]; larger connected pieces are split by a vertex separator taken from a BFS level structure rooted at a pseudo-peripheral vertex (the level near the middle with the best size/balance trade-off, pruned of vertices without neighbours on the far side); separators are numbered after both halves.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_overlap_save_plan_apply" => "Compute the full linear convolution of a real recording with the prepared filter. The output has sample units times tap units. Empty recordings give an empty measured tensor. The result has at most 262144 values. Applies the filter with zero extension and returns the full convolution. # Errors Errors on non-finite inputs or output, or an unallocatable output extent.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_overlap_save_plan_apply_batch" => "Convolve up to 4096 real recordings sharing one sample dimension. Supply flat samples and zero-based row offsets; repeated offsets represent empty recordings. Returns output offsets and flat values with sample units times tap units. The whole batch has at most 262144 output values. Applies this prepared filter to several recordings in input order. Each result has the same length and zero extension as [`Self::apply`]. Empty recordings give empty results. Independent recordings can run in parallel under the active execution policy. # Errors Returns the error for the first recording that fails [`Self::apply`].\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_overlap_save_plan_new" => "Prepare the spectrum of a measured real filter with at most 65536 taps. The immutable handle retains the tap units and can be reused for several recordings in this session. Creates a plan for a real finite impulse response filter. # Errors Errors for an empty or non-finite filter, a non-finite transform or an unallocatable FFT extent.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_par_for_chunks_mut" => "Native disjoint mutable chunk scheduling specializes mutation to returning a replacement vector of identical chunk length and units, including the short final chunk. Checked owner-thread callbacks preserve failure and budget semantics. Runs `f(i, row)` over mutable chunks of `data` of `chunk` elements each (`i` is the chunk index); sequential when there are fewer than `grain` chunks. The chunks are disjoint, so the result cannot depend on the scheduling.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_par_for_each_mut" => "Native mutable parallel map specializes mutation to returning a replacement value. The input tensor is owned/copied; outputs retain identical physical units and original index semantics. Runs `f(i, &mut items[i])` for every element, in parallel when there are at least `grain` elements. Each element is touched by exactly one call, so the outcome is independent of the scheduling.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_par_map_indexed" => "Actual native parallel map with host callbacks serviced serially on their owning thread. Index order and native Rayon scheduling are retained; every worker is joined and callback failures/budgets are propagated. Maps `0..n` through `f` and collects in index order. Runs sequentially when `n < grain` (or `n < 2`).\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_par_map_slice" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Maps the elements of `items` through `f` and collects in order.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_par_sum_fixed" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Sum of `f(i)` over `0..n` with a fixed association order: the terms are added sequentially inside blocks of `block` indices and the block sums are then added sequentially in block order. The result is bit-identical for every thread count (and for the sequential path).\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_partial_derivative_scaled" => "Native finite-difference calculus with physical reference scales: point,coordinate_scale,value_scale,max_evaluations,[partial index or Jacobian output count],callback. Independent D/E units; derivative E/D, Hessian/Laplacian E/D^2. References are positive. Shared callback errors and finite evaluation budgets are preserved. Central-difference partial derivative of `f` with respect to coordinate `index` at `point`. Returns NaN when `index` is out of range.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_pchip_derivative" => "Portable native approximation model with independent coordinate and ordinate dimensions. Every query checks kind/version, defining data lengths, finite data, monotone grids where required, interval and allocation budgets. Derivatives restore ordinate/coordinate powers; integrals restore their product. Model values contain only defining data and no process-local references. Derivative at `x`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_pchip_eval" => "Portable native approximation model with independent coordinate and ordinate dimensions. Every query checks kind/version, defining data lengths, finite data, monotone grids where required, interval and allocation budgets. Derivatives restore ordinate/coordinate powers; integrals restore their product. Model values contain only defining data and no process-local references. Value at `x`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_pchip_new" => "Portable native approximation model with independent coordinate and ordinate dimensions. Every query checks kind/version, defining data lengths, finite data, monotone grids where required, interval and allocation budgets. Derivatives restore ordinate/coordinate powers; integrals restore their product. Model values contain only defining data and no process-local references. Builds the interpolant. # Errors [`ApproxError::Invalid`] for non-finite data, mismatched lengths, fewer than two samples, or non-increasing coordinates.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_poisson_dist_cdf" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Returns the cumulative distribution function (CDF) value at `k`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_poisson_dist_new" => "Checked native legacy distribution. Continuous parameters and queries retain coherent physical units; inverse CDF restores sample units and PDF has inverse sample units. Creates a new `PoissonDist` instance. # Errors Returns an error if `rate <= 0.0`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_poisson_dist_pmf" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Returns the probability mass function (PMF) value at `k`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_poly_gf256_degree" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Returns the degree of the polynomial.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_poly_gf256_derivative" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Returns the derivative of the polynomial over GF(2^8). In GF(2^8), the derivative has a special property: d/dx(x^n) = n * x^(n-1), where n is reduced mod 2. Thus, only odd-power terms contribute to the derivative.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_poly_gf256_eval" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Evaluates the polynomial at a given point using Horner's method. # Arguments * `x` - The evaluation point in GF(2^8). # Returns The value p(x) in GF(2^8).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_poly_gf256_new" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Creates a new polynomial from coefficients. # Arguments * `coeffs` - Coefficients in ascending order of powers (`coeffs[i]` is the coefficient of `x^i`).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_poly_gf256_normalize" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Normalizes the polynomial by removing zero coefficients of the highest powers (the trailing elements in ascending order).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_poly_gf256_poly_add" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Adds two polynomials over GF(2^8). In GF(2^8), addition is XOR.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_poly_gf256_poly_div" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Divides two polynomials over GF(2^8). # Arguments * `divisor` - The divisor polynomial. # Returns A tuple (quotient, remainder), or an error if divisor is zero. # Errors Returns an error if the divisor polynomial is empty (zero polynomial).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_poly_gf256_poly_mul" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Multiplies two polynomials over GF(2^8).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_poly_gf256_poly_sub" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Subtracts two polynomials over GF(2^8). In GF(2^8), subtraction is the same as addition (XOR).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_poly_gf256_scale" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Scales the polynomial by a constant in GF(2^8).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_polynomial_normalized_new" => "Native polynomial in explicitly normalized dimensionless coordinate u, highest degree first. Real-root methods require an explicit positive coordinate reference and restore physical roots/tolerances. Creates a new `Polynomial` from coefficients (highest degree first).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_polynomial_system_new" => "Normalized polynomial coefficients describe F(x/coordinate_reference)/residual_reference; two positive references preserve independent physical coordinate and residual dimensions. Maximum6variables/4096terms/256total-degree paths.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_prime_field_inverse" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Computes the multiplicative inverse of the element. The inverse `x` of an element `a` is such that `a * x = 1 (mod modulus)`. This implementation uses the Extended Euclidean Algorithm. # Returns * `Some(PrimeFieldElement)` containing the inverse if it exists. * `None` if the element is not invertible (i.e., its value is not coprime to the modulus).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_prime_field_is_agnostic" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Returns `true` for a modulus-agnostic element (see the type docs).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_prime_field_new" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Creates a new `PrimeFieldElement`. The initial value is reduced modulo the `modulus`. # Arguments * `value` - The initial value of the element. * `modulus` - The prime modulus of the field.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_prime_field_pow" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Computes (self^exp) modulo modulus.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_charpoly" => "Return the exact characteristic polynomial coefficients in ascending degree, including the leading one. The normalized QMatrix must be square. Computes the characteristic polynomial of a square rational matrix. Returns the coefficients of \$\\\\det(\\\\lambda I - A)\$ in ascending powers, from the constant term `c_0` to the leading coefficient `c_n = 1`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_det" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The determinant of a square matrix.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_det_bareiss" => "Return the exact determinant of a square normalized QMatrix with integer coefficients, using fraction-free Bareiss elimination. Fraction-free Bareiss determinant of a square integer matrix over \$\\\\mathbb{Z}\$. Uses exact integer division by the previous step's pivot (`(a[i][j] * pivot - a[i][k] * a[k][j]) / prev_pivot`) without any rational GCD reductions.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_det_modular_int" => "Return the exact determinant of a square normalized QMatrix with integer coefficients, using modular elimination and Chinese remaindering. Multi-prime modular determinant of a square integer matrix over \$\\\\mathbb{Z}\$ using 62-bit Montgomery `GF(p)` Gaussian elimination and Garner CRT reconstruction.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_hermite_normal_form" => "Return the row-style Hermite normal form of a normalized QMatrix with integer coefficients. Row-style Hermite Normal Form (HNF) of an integer matrix over \$\\\\mathbb{Z}\$. Brings `m` by unimodular row operations into upper-echelon Hermite normal form \$H\$ where every leading non-zero pivot \$H_{r, c} > 0\$ and all entries above a pivot satisfy \$0 \\\\le H_{i, c} < H_{r, c}\$.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_hermite_normal_form_with_transform" => "Return the row-style Hermite normal form and unimodular row transform satisfying transform * A = form. Row-style Hermite Normal Form \$(H, U)\$ of an integer matrix over \$\\\\mathbb{Z}\$ satisfying \$U A = H\$ with \$U\$ unimodular (\$\\\\det U = \\\\pm 1\$).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_identity" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The identity matrix of size `n`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_inverse" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The inverse of a square matrix.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_is_zero_vec" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Whether a vector is zero.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_matmul" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The product of two matrices (`a` is `r x m`, `b` is `m x c`).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_matvec" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The product of a matrix and a vector.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_nullspace" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. A basis of `{x : m x = 0}` for `m` with `cols` columns.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_q" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The integer `n` as a rational.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_rank" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The rank of a matrix whose rows have length `cols`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_reduce_mod" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Reduces `v` modulo the span of the echelon rows `basis` (with their `pivots`, as returned by [`rref`]): the remainder vanishes exactly on the span.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_rref" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Brings `m` (rows of length `cols`) to reduced row echelon form in place, drops the zero rows and returns the pivot columns.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_smith_normal_form" => "Return the Smith normal form and unimodular transforms satisfying left * A * right = form.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_smith_normal_form_diag" => "Return the positive nonzero Smith invariant factors in divisibility order. The normalized QMatrix must have integer coefficients. Computes the non-zero diagonal invariant factors \$[`d_1`, `d_2`, \\\\dots, `d_r`]\$ of the Smith Normal Form of an integer matrix over \$\\\\mathbb{Z}\$, with \$`d_i` > 0\$ and \$`d_1` \\\\mid `d_2` \\\\mid \\\\dots \\\\mid `d_r`\$.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_solve" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. A particular solution of `m x = b`, with free variables set to zero. Returns `None` for an inconsistent system, a mismatched right-hand side, or an invalid matrix shape. Pivots are chosen from left to right.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_solve_dixon" => "Solve an exact square system by Dixon lifting and residual certification. A singular system returns None. Solves a nonsingular square system \$A x = b\$ over \$\\\\mathbb{Q}\$ using Dixon's \$p\$-adic lifting over a 62-bit prime \$p\$ and exact residual certification. Returns `None` if `a` is not square, dimensions mismatch, or `a` is singular.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_solve_mat" => "Solve an exact system with multiple right-hand sides. Free variables are zero, and inconsistent systems return None. Solves a matrix linear system \$A X = B\$ where \$A\$ has `cols` columns and `B` has matching row count. Free variables in underdetermined systems are set to zero. Uses Dixon \$p\$-adic lifting for square nonsingular systems of order \$n \\\\ge 6\$ and sparse-pivot elimination otherwise.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_solve_unique" => "Solve an exact system with full column rank. Inconsistent and underdetermined systems return None. Solves `m * x = b` over `Q` when the system has a unique solution (full column rank `cols`), returning `None` if inconsistent or underdetermined.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_span_basis" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. A basis (reduced echelon rows) of the span of `vectors` of length `dim`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_transpose" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The transpose of an `r x c` matrix.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qlinalg_zeros" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The zero vector of length `n`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qmatrix_export" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qmatrix_new" => "Construct exact rational coefficient algebra after explicit division by a same-unit positive reference. All subsequent Q operations are normalized coefficient-space operations; physical scales are retained by the caller rather than silently erased. Finite Float inputs are converted to their exact binary rational values.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qs_factor" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Finds a non-trivial divisor of the odd composite `n`. Returns `Some(d)` with `1 < d < n` and `d | n`, or `None` for invalid input, for a prime, when `n` has more than [`QsLimits::MAX_DIGITS`] decimal digits, when the relation matrix would exceed [`QsLimits::MAX_FACTOR_BASE_COLUMNS`], and when the polynomial or [`QsLimits::max_sieve_positions`] budget is exhausted. An even `n > 2` returns `2` directly. The input may contain small factors: trial division by the primes below 1000 runs first and returns a factor directly. The digit limit is checked before that trial division, so an oversized request never does any sieving work. Perfect powers, prime input and even input are otherwise handled before the sieve. The limits are not clamped upwards or downwards to hide a bad choice: they are used as given, apart from a safety clamp on `bound` and `interval`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qs_factor_pair" => "Finds two ordered nontrivial exact factors within the quadratic sieve limits and verifies their product. The input and both factors are dimensionless integers. None means no pair was found within the supplied limits. Splits `n` into two proper factors in ascending order. Uses the same limits and early factor checks as [`qs_factor`]. The product of the returned factors is exactly `n`. Either may be composite.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qs_factor_with" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. [`qs_factor`] with an explicit configuration and run statistics. The same guarantees hold: the returned divisor is always in `(1, n)` and divides `n`; `None` means \"no factor found\", not \"n is composite\" or \"n is prime\".\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qs_is_probable_prime" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. A Baillie-PSW probable-prime test. Deterministic Miller-Rabin with the first twelve prime bases for machine words (which is a proof for all of `u64`), and a base-2 strong probable-prime test plus a strong Lucas test with Selfridge's parameters for larger integers. No composite is known to pass the latter, in particular the smallest strong pseudoprime to those twelve Miller-Rabin bases (318665857834031151167461) does not.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qs_limits_for_digits" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Parameter set for a `digits`-digit number. The factor-base bound is the standard QS optimum `L_n[1/2, 1/2] = exp(0.5 sqrt(ln n ln ln n))`, rounded up to two significant digits; the sieve interval is of the same order. The large-prime multiplier grows with the size, the relation margin is a small fraction of the estimated factor-base width, and the work bound is `L_n[1/2, 1] = exp(sqrt(ln n ln ln n))` capped at `2 * 10^10` positions so that even a hopeless input has a bounded cost. For 80 digits this yields a factor base around five million and a sieve interval of two million, which is beyond the column limit: the attempt returns `None` before allocating the sieve. At 65 digits the matrix is already large (tens of thousands of columns and hundreds of megabytes at the peak), but the work bound still terminates. Beyond about 66 digits the factor base typically exceeds the column limit. The remaining primes are checked for direct divisors before the attempt returns.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_qs_limits_new" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_quantum_double_slit_scenario" => "IO: execute the original reduced-unit 256 by 256, 300-step double-slit demonstration and write the NPY density. Provide an explicit grid-update budget. An example scenario simulating a wave packet hitting a double slit. # Errors This function will return an error if the underlying `run_schrodinger_simulation` fails or if the final state cannot be written to the NPY file. The last sampled density is saved as `schrodinger_double_slit.npy` inside `output_dir`, which is created if missing.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_quantum_run_schrodinger" => "Advances the two-dimensional periodic Schrödinger model with a positive time increment. Input lengths, mass, reduced Planck constant and potential use SI dimensions. Returns inverse-length final amplitudes, inverse-square-length density after steps 1, 11, 21 and so on, and their measured times. Samples have the x coordinate varying fastest. Evolves the periodic 2D wave by Strang splitting and returns density frames. Frames are sampled after steps 1, 11, 21, and so on. Each frame has `ny` rows and `nx` columns. On success the supplied wave becomes the final state. # Errors Invalid geometry or samples, an unrepresentable phase, wave or density, failed allocations, or cancellation.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_quantum_schrodinger_plan_evolve" => "Evolves a complex wavefunction with inverse-length amplitudes on a prepared periodic grid. The input and final_psi are flattened with x varying fastest. Returns the final wavefunction and time equal to steps multiplied by the signed time increment. Zero steps preserve the initial wave. Uniform potentials can evolve directly to the final state. Returns the final wave and optionally streams earlier wave samples. With a stride `s`, the observer sees completed steps `1, 1 + s, ...` within the requested interval. A zero step count emits no samples. Pass `None` for final-state-only evolution. A uniform potential can then be advanced directly in one pair of Fourier transforms. # Errors Invalid initial samples or shape, an unrepresentable evolved state, failed allocations, cancellation or an error from the observer.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_quantum_schrodinger_plan_new" => "Prepares periodic two-dimensional Strang split-step evolution for repeated wavefunctions. Supply positive lengths, mass and reduced Planck constant in physical units, a signed measured time increment, and one energy sample per grid point in x-fast order. Every grid extent is positive. A zero increment gives the identity. Prepares the signed time increment, grid and physical potential. The evolution call supplies the step count. The `time_steps` field controls the legacy snapshot-returning entry point. # Errors Returns an error for invalid geometry or coefficients, an unrepresentable phase angle, or failure to reserve phase storage.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_real_roots_find_roots" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Finds numerical real roots of the polynomial in ascending order. Root isolation and refinement reuse the same Sturm chain. When distinct roots stay together in a bracket narrower than `tolerance`, the method returns one representative for that cluster. # Errors Invalid coefficients or tolerance, an unrepresentable root bound or Sturm chain, or failure to isolate or refine a bracket.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_real_roots_find_roots_in" => "Finds real roots of a normalized polynomial within the finite closed interval [lower, upper], including endpoint roots. The bounds, absolute tolerance and positive coordinate reference share one physical dimension. The sorted root vector retains that dimension. Finds numerical real roots in the finite closed interval `[left, right]`. Includes roots at either endpoint and returns results in ascending order. Endpoint checks use the original binary coefficients. Only the requested interval is searched, with the tolerance and cluster behavior of [`find_roots`]. # Errors Non-finite or reversed endpoints, invalid coefficients or tolerance, or a Sturm chain that cannot resolve the requested interval.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_real_roots_isolate_real_roots" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Isolates the numerical real roots of a polynomial in ascending order. Intervals are closed. A bracket may be wider than `precision` if its Sturm count is one. Roots that stay together in a bracket narrower than `precision` are returned as one cluster interval. # Errors Invalid coefficients or precision, an unrepresentable root bound or Sturm chain, or failure to separate adjacent brackets in floating point.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_real_roots_refine_root_bisection" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Refines one isolated root in a closed interval by Sturm bisection. Returns NaN for invalid endpoints, tolerance, polynomial or root counts. If the width cannot be reduced further in floating point, returns an endpoint of the last bracket.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_real_roots_sturm_sequence" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Generates the Sturm sequence for a numerical polynomial. The Sturm sequence is a sequence of polynomials derived from the original polynomial and its derivative. It is used to determine the number of distinct real roots of a polynomial in a given interval. # Arguments * `poly` - The input polynomial as a `Polynomial`. # Returns A `Vec<Polynomial>` representing the Sturm sequence.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_circular_orbit" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Circular equatorial orbit `(E, L, Omega)` at radius `r` (`None` if none exists).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_frame" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_frame_normalized" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_geodesic_circular" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Circular equatorial timelike orbit at radius `r`. # Errors Fails if no circular orbit exists at `r`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_geodesic_constraint" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Value of the constraint residual `H + mu^2/2` (zero on the mass shell).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_geodesic_from_init" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. As [`Geodesic::new`] with the initial data bundled in a [`GeodesicInit`]. # Errors Fails when the constraint has no real solution (forbidden region).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_geodesic_integrate" => "Advances a retained geodesic by up to 65,536 nonzero signed implicit-midpoint steps. Supply Time and ordered positive stopping radii in a physical frame or numerical values in a normalized frame. Returns a record with termination (Steps, Horizon or Escaped) and the final state in frame units. The project flag requests mass-shell projection. Integration and unit conversion must succeed before the retained handle is updated.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_geodesic_new" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Starts a geodesic at `(r, theta, phi)` with conserved `E`, `L`, polar momentum and radial direction (`radial_sign = +-1`), solving the mass-shell constraint for `p_r`. # Errors Fails when the constraint has no real solution (forbidden region).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_geodesic_state" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_geodesic_step" => "Advances a retained geodesic by one nonzero signed implicit-midpoint step. Supply Time in a physical frame or an affine step in a normalized frame. The project flag projects the new momentum onto the mass shell. Returns the new state in frame units. The proper_time field carries the affine parameter, which is proper time for a unit timelike mass shell. Integration and unit conversion must succeed before the retained handle is updated.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_hamiltonian" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Hamiltonian `1/2 g^{mu nu} p p` at `(r, theta)` with momenta `(p_r, p_theta)`, energy and angular momentum.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_horizon" => "Returns the optional outer Kerr–Newman horizon radius. The result is a measured Length in a physical frame and a Float in a normalized frame. A superextremal metric has no horizon and returns None. The adapter restores the radius without requiring an intermediate normalized radius to fit in Float when the physical result is representable.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_isco" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Innermost stable circular orbit: the minimum of `E(r)` over timelike circular orbits.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_metric" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_orbit_cos_theta" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. `cos(theta)` at Mino time `lambda`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_orbit_frequencies" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Fundamental frequencies: `(Upsilon_r, Upsilon_theta, Upsilon_phi, Gamma)` in Mino time (`Upsilon_theta = 0` for equatorial orbits, where `theta` is constant) and the coordinate-time frequencies `(Omega_r, Omega_theta, Omega_phi)`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_orbit_from_apsides" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Orbit specified by periapsis `r_p`, apoapsis `r_a` and the turning latitude `z_minus = cos(theta_min)` (`0` = equatorial); `prograde` selects the sign of `L`. The constants `(E, L, Q)` are found by Newton iteration. The orbit starts at periapsis on the equator-crossing side of the polar motion. # Errors Fails if the iteration does not converge or the resulting orbit is not bound.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_orbit_new" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Closed-form bound geodesic with constants `(E, L, Q)` starting at `(r0, theta0, phi0)`; `radial_out` / `polar_down` give the signs of `dr/dlambda` and of `dtheta/dlambda` (`polar_down`: theta increasing, i.e. moving toward the south pole). # Errors Fails unless `E < 1`, the radial polynomial has four real roots with `r1 > r2 > r3`, `r2` is outside the horizon, `r0` lies in `[r2, r1]` and the polar motion is allowed.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_orbit_polar_period" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Mino period of the polar motion (`None` for equatorial orbits).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_orbit_radial_period" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Mino period of the radial motion.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_orbit_radius" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Radius at Mino time `lambda` (measured from the start of the orbit).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_orbit_state" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. State `(t, r, theta, phi)` at Mino time `lambda` (`t = 0` and `phi = phi0` at the start).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_photon_orbit" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Radius of the circular equatorial photon orbit strictly outside the outer horizon. The positive angular direction is selected by `prograde`. A branch that coincides with the horizon, has no exterior root, or cannot be represented returns `None`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_photon_radius" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Radius of the circular equatorial photon orbit of Kerr (`prograde` or retrograde).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_schild_advance" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Advances the geodesic by the affine parameter `dtau_total` with an adaptive Dormand-Prince 5(4) integrator (relative tolerance `tol`). Returns `false` if the radius fell below `r_stop` (the state is left at the last accepted step).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_schild_angular_momentum" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Conserved axial angular momentum `L_z = x p_y - y p_x`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_schild_boyer_lindquist" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Boyer-Lindquist `(r, theta, phi)` of the position (outside the horizon).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_schild_carter_constant" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Carter constant `Q = p_theta^2 + cos^2 theta [a^2 (mu^2 - E^2) + L^2/sin^2 theta]` of the current state (off the axis).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_schild_energy" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Conserved energy `E = -p_t`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_schild_hamiltonian" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Mass-shell value `1/2 g^{mu nu} p_mu p_nu` (equals `-mu^2/2`).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_schild_new" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Starts a geodesic from Boyer-Lindquist data: position `(r, theta, phi)`, constants of motion `(E, L, Q)`, mass-shell value `mu2` (1 timelike, 0 null) and the signs of `dr/d tau` and `d theta / d tau`. # Errors Fails if the position is inside the horizon, on the axis, or the motion is forbidden there.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_schild_radius" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Kerr radius of the current position.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_schwarzschild" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Schwarzschild black hole.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_shadow_analytic" => "Kerr shadow for a distant off-axis observer. Mass and spin use geometrized lengths, theta is in radians, and points is the sample count per half (2 through 2048). Returns a [2*points, 2] tensor of alpha and beta in the frame length units.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_trace_ray" => "Trace one Kerr null geodesic from the given observer radius and inclination in radians. Mass, spin, radius and xi use frame lengths and eta uses squared lengths. Returns Captured or Escaped with dimensionless arrival angles. Traces a null geodesic backwards from the observer. The impact parameters are `xi = L/E`, `eta = Q/E^2` from the observer at `(r_o, theta_o)` inwards (initial direction: decreasing `r`, polar motion toward larger `theta` if `polar_down`) by integrating the Mino-time equations with RK4. # Errors Fails if the ray is not allowed at the observer (`R(r_o) < 0` or `Theta(theta_o) < 0`), the step budget is exhausted.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_trace_shadow" => "Find the Kerr shadow by tracing up to 64 regularly spaced image-plane directions. Mass, spin and observer radius use frame lengths and inclination is in radians. Returns a [points, 2] tensor in frame length units in increasing image angle.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_unbound_advance" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Advances the geodesic by the Mino time `dlambda` with an adaptive Dormand-Prince 5(4) integrator (relative tolerance `tol`). Returns `false` if the orbit reached the horizon (the state is left at the last accepted step).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_unbound_carter_constant" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Carter constant measured from the current state, `Q = p_theta^2 + cos^2 theta [a^2 (mu^2 - E^2) + L^2 / sin^2 theta]` (off the axis).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_unbound_impact_parameter" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Impact parameter `b = L / sqrt(E^2 - mu^2)` (`None` for a parabolic orbit `E^2 = mu^2`).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_unbound_new" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Starts a geodesic with constants `(E, L, Q)` at `(r, theta, phi)`; `radial_out` / `polar_down` give the signs of `dr/dlambda` and of `dtheta/dlambda`. # Errors Fails unless `M > 0`, `|a| < M`, `Q >= 0`, `0 < E`, `E^2 >= mu^2` (an orbit that can reach infinity), `r` is outside the horizon and both potentials allow the motion there.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_unbound_normalisation" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Normalisation `g_{mu nu} u^mu u^nu` of the current state, from `Sigma g^{mu nu} p_mu p_nu = -mu^2` with `p_t = -E`, `p_phi = L`, `p_r = dr/dlambda` and `p_theta = dtheta/dlambda`; it equals `-mu^2` on a geodesic.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_unbound_scatter" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. Runs the orbit from its (inward) start until it either falls through the horizon or returns to its starting radius moving outward. The azimuth is completed analytically: the two legs still missing between the start radius and infinity contribute `b (u0 + u1)` to leading order, so the start radius has to be large compared with the impact parameter. # Errors Fails if the state does not move inward, if the orbit is parabolic (`E^2 = mu^2`) or if the step budget is exhausted.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_relativity_unbound_state" => "Native geometrized relativity with positive length reference. Mass, spin and charge metric parameters use geometric lengths; coordinate/proper time restore seconds, Mino time uses inverse length, specific energy and angles are dimensionless. State `(t, r, theta, phi)`; `t = 0` and `phi = phi0` at the start.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_release" => "Session-local reverse AD object. Tape constructor reserves 1..65536 nodes. Linear quantity values use coherent units; addition requires matching dimensions, products/quotients and gradients propagate physical powers; transcendental arguments must be dimensionless. Opaque handles are kind checked, invalid across sessions and after release. Release dependent variables/gradients before their tape. Callbacks scope temporary handles. No native pointer/state is serialized.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_reverse_gradient_scaled" => "Exact native AD with normalized callback variables and independent physical references: point,positive coordinate_scale,positive value_scale,max_evaluations,callback. Forward callback scalar duals are {val,deriv}; vector duals are {val:vector,deriv:vector}; all dual arithmetic is dimensionless and uses native num_dual_* operators. Reverse callbacks use checked NativeAdVar handles on an ephemeral session tape; native operations enforce same-tape identity and a65536-node limit. Output derivatives restore E/D; no numerical differencing or opaque-callback finite-difference fallback. Exact value and gradient `(f(x), grad f(x))` of `f(&[Var]) -> Var` at `x` in a single reverse-mode pass. # Errors [`AdError::Empty`] when `x` is empty.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_richardson_derivative_scaled" => "Native finite-difference calculus with physical reference scales: point,coordinate_scale,value_scale,max_evaluations,[partial index or Jacobian output count],callback. Independent D/E units; derivative E/D, Hessian/Laplacian E/D^2. References are positive. Shared callback errors and finite evaluation budgets are preserved. The first derivative of `f` at `x`, by a central difference with one Richardson extrapolation step.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_rigid_md_controls" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rigid_md_dof" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Degrees of freedom: 3 translations plus the non-degenerate rotations, minus the 3 of the total momentum.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rigid_md_kinetic_energy" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Translational plus rotational kinetic energy.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rigid_md_max_geometry_error" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Maximum deviation of any intramolecular site distance from its rigid value (diagnostic).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rigid_md_momentum" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Total linear momentum.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rigid_md_new" => "Construct the actual native rigid-molecule site driver. Checked CSR partitions identify rigid molecules; the physical forcefield is transferred once. Unitful centers/sites, translational and rotational DOFs retain mass-length-time dimensions; rotational integration remains native. Builds the rigid-body state from the site positions and velocities in `sys`. `molecules[m]` lists the site indices of molecule `m`; the lists must partition the sites. The current site positions must already form rigid molecules (their shape defines the body frame); velocities are projected onto rigid motion. # Errors Fails if the molecules do not partition the sites or the box is not fully periodic.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rigid_md_pressure_tensor" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Molecular pressure tensor `(sum M v v + W_mol) / V` with the virial of the centre-of-mass separations (site virial minus the intramolecular lever arms).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rigid_md_run" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Runs `n` steps using one rotor composition for the entire run. # Errors Propagates the errors of [`Self::step`]. Completed steps remain applied.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rigid_md_state" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rigid_md_step" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Advances the centre of mass by velocity Verlet and applies the selected rotor composition. # Errors Invalid rotation order or non-finite step times are reported before state updates. A force-field error during propagation can leave the state partially advanced.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rigid_md_sync_sites" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Writes site positions and velocities from the rigid-body state.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rigid_md_temperature" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Instantaneous temperature.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rigid_md_total_energy" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Total energy.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rigorous_ball_contains" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Whether the point `(re, im)` lies in every component of the box.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rigorous_ball_distance" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The largest distance from the centre to `(re, im)` over the components.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rigorous_ball_enclosure" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rng_below" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Uniform integer in `0..n` (`n > 0`), without modulo bias.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rng_beta" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Beta sample with positive finite shapes `a` and `b`. Invalid shapes give NaN.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rng_binomial" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Binomial sample with `n` trials and a probability in `[0, 1]`. Degenerate probabilities give 0 or `n`. Invalid probabilities give 0.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rng_exponential" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Exponential sample with a positive finite rate. Invalid rates give NaN.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rng_fill_normal" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Fills `out` with standard normal samples.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rng_gamma" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Gamma sample with positive finite shape `k` and scale `theta`. Invalid parameters give NaN.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rng_jump" => "Advance the session-owned random generator by 2^128 raw steps and clear its cached normal sample. Returns true when the generator was updated. Advances the raw stream by `2^128` steps and clears the cached normal.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rng_long_jump" => "Advance the session-owned random generator by 2^192 raw steps and clear its cached normal sample. Returns true when the generator was updated. Advances the raw stream by `2^192` steps and clears the cached normal.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rng_new" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Creates a generator from a 64-bit seed.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rng_next_u64" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Next raw 64-bit output.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rng_normal" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Standard normal sample (Box-Muller, caches the second value).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rng_normal_with" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Normal sample with the given mean and standard deviation.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rng_poisson" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Poisson sample by Knuth's algorithm at small means and gamma splitting at large means. NaN and nonpositive means give zero. Positive means or results outside the `u64` range saturate.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rng_shuffle" => "Fisher-Yates specialization over arbitrary owned kernel Values. Element representations, physical unit witnesses and opaque handles are preserved; only the order is mutated in local owned storage. Fisher-Yates shuffle in place.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rng_uniform" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Uniform sample in `[0, 1)` with 53 random bits.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rng_uniform_range" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Uniform sample in `[a, b)`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_robust_bootstrap_ci" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Percentile bootstrap confidence interval for `statistic` at level `1 - alpha`, with `resamples` seeded resamples. Calls `statistic` once per resample in draw order and excludes NaN replicates from the interval.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_root_system_all_weights" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. All weights with multiplicity (dominant weights and their Weyl orbits); `None` if there are more than `cap` of them.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_root_system_casimir" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The Casimir eigenvalue `(L, L + 2 rho)` of the irreducible representation of highest weight `L`, with long roots of squared length 2. Uses dimensionless Dynkin labels. Returns `None` for a reducible root system or a label count different from its rank. Signed labels also evaluate the same quadratic expression.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_root_system_coxeter_number" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The Coxeter number `2 N / n` (irreducible systems only).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_root_system_dimension" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The dimension `n + 2 N` of the Lie algebra.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_root_system_dominant_multiplicities" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The multiplicities of the dominant weights of the irreducible representation of highest weight `top`, by Freudenthal's formula; `None` for reducible systems or when more than `cap` dominant weights occur.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_root_system_dual_coxeter_number" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The dual Coxeter number `1 + (theta, rho)` (irreducible systems only).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_root_system_dynkin_index" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The Dynkin index `dim(V) C(V) / dim(g)` (the fundamental of `su(n)` has index 1, the adjoint `2 h^vee`). Requires an irreducible root system and one nonnegative dimensionless Dynkin label per simple root.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_root_system_exponents" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The exponents: the dual partition of the numbers of roots of each height.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_root_system_fundamental_weights" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The fundamental weights in simple-root coordinates (rows of the inverse Cartan matrix).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_root_system_gram" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The Gram matrix `(alpha_i, alpha_j)` of the simple roots.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_root_system_highest_root" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The highest root (irreducible systems only).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_root_system_inner" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The inner product of two weights given by Dynkin labels.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_root_system_is_irreducible" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Whether the Dynkin diagram is connected.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_root_system_new" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The root system of a Cartan matrix of finite type.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_root_system_num_positive" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The number of positive roots.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_root_system_tensor" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The decomposition of `V(a) ⊗ V(b)` into irreducibles (Brauer-Klimyk): `(highest weight, multiplicity)` pairs.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_root_system_weight_multiplicity" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The multiplicity of the weight `w` (any weight) in the irreducible representation of highest weight `top`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_root_system_weyl_dim" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The exact dimension for a highest weight with dimensionless Dynkin labels. Returns `None` unless there is one nonnegative integer label per simple root.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_root_system_weyl_order" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. The order of the Weyl group, `prod (e_i + 1)`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rs_encoder_encode" => "Encodes a tensor of exact bytes using a retained Reed–Solomon encoder. The result begins with the original bytes and ends with the prepared parity count. Input and output have no physical units. Encodes `message` as data followed by parity bytes. # Errors Returns an error if the combined output exceeds 255 symbols.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rs_encoder_new" => "Prepares a Reed–Solomon encoder for the supplied number of parity bytes. The session-owned encoder retains the generator's feedback table and accepts blocks of at most 255 bytes including parity. Prepares the generator's feedback rows for a given parity length. # Errors More than 255 parity symbols cannot fit in a block.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_rs_encoder_parity_symbols" => "Returns the exact parity-byte count of a retained Reed–Solomon encoder. Returns this encoder's parity length.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_scalar_float_add" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_scalar_float_atan2" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_scalar_float_call" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_scalar_float_compare" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_scalar_float_constant" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_scalar_float_div" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_scalar_float_mul" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_scalar_float_nan" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_scalar_float_neg" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_scalar_float_powf" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_scalar_float_powi" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_scalar_float_select" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_scalar_float_sub" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_scalar_float_to_f64" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_scalar_float_unary" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_scalar_from_extern1" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_scalar_from_extern2" => "Native normalized IEEE scalar operation. NaN/interval-entire sentinels retain their native meaning; no physical quantity units are erased.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_scenario_run" => "Execute the actual native named scenario with bounded JSON parameters. The contract must be native-schema: JSON numbers use the units documented by that scenario's schema and preserve native defaults. Typed physical quantity APIs are separately exposed for each numerical engine. Runs the scenario `name` with parameters given as a JSON object and returns its results as JSON. Arrays are encoded the way `ndarray` serialises them: `{\"v\": 1, \"dim\": [rows, cols], \"data\": [...]}`. # Errors An unknown scenario, parameters that do not parse, or a failure of the simulation itself.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_scenario_run_many" => "Execute actual native parallel run_many over bounded named JSON requests. Input records have name and parameters strings; per-request native Ok/Err results and request order are preserved, with invalid requests rejected before native allocation. Runs independent scenarios `(name, params)` and returns their results in request order. Every request is evaluated exactly as by [`run`]; the requests share nothing, so the result is the same as `requests.iter().map(run)` for any thread count (scenarios that take an explicit `seed` are reproducible; unseeded stochastic ones are as random as in [`run`]). Nested parallelism inside a scenario runs on the same rayon pool (work stealing).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_schema_catalog" => "Serialize the actual native scenario catalog, including physical unit notes and defaults; this discovery operator does not substitute for scenario execution. The catalog of every scenario (see the module documentation).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_schema_catalog_json" => "Read the native scenario catalog JSON including parameter defaults and unit notes. [`catalog`] as JSON text, the form a host reads.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_schema_infer" => "Infer the actual native scenario field type from a bounded JSON value; result is the native serialized FieldType enum. Infers the type of a JSON value.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_schema_parse_type" => "Parse native schema type syntax and return its serialized native FieldType enum if valid. Parses the catalog's type notation of [`Note::ty`]: `bool`, `int`, `float`, `str`, `choice`, a trailing `[]` per tensor axis, a trailing `?` for an optional value.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_schema_witness" => "Execute every actual native scenario on its declared example/default request and infer output schemas. All examples are preflighted against one explicit aggregate work budget before execution. Runs every scenario on its request and infers the shape of its result (the content of `scenario_results.json`). Independent scenarios use the active execution pool, and the first failure is reported in catalog order. # Errors A scenario failed on its own defaults or example.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_second_derivative_scaled" => "Native finite-difference calculus with physical reference scales: point,coordinate_scale,value_scale,max_evaluations,[partial index or Jacobian output count],callback. Independent D/E units; derivative E/D, Hessian/Laplacian E/D^2. References are positive. Shared callback errors and finite evaluation budgets are preserved. The second derivative of `f` at `x`.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_second_order_check_scaled" => "Native scaled global/constrained optimization with shared actual host evaluation limit. Nelder: x,xscale,yscale,step,tol,iterations,budget,f. Differential evolution: lo,hi,xscale,yscale,population,generations,budget,seed,f. Annealing: x,xscale,yscale,step,temperature,cooling,iterations,budget,seed,f. Constrained: x,xscale,yscale,equality_scale,inequality_scale,tol,iterations,budget,f,eq,ineq. Constraints independently carry C/H units; SQP returns physical multipliers E/C and E/H, native status and second-order verdict. Second-order: x,lambda,mu,xscale,yscale,eqscale,ineqscale,budget,f,eq,ineq. No global-optimality claim; native iteration/status semantics retained. Second-order sufficiency check at a KKT point `x`. Builds the dense Hessian of the Lagrangian `L = f + sum_i lambda_i h_i + sum_j mu_j g_j` by central differences of `L` itself (so no analytic gradient is required), projects it onto the null space of the active constraint Jacobian and tests the reduced Hessian for positive definiteness. Active inequalities are those with `g_j(x)` at least `-1e-8` or with a strictly positive reported multiplier. Returns [`SecondOrderStatus::Sufficient`] when the smallest eigenvalue of the reduced Hessian is larger than a finite-difference margin, and [`SecondOrderStatus::NotSufficient`] when it is more negative than that margin. Returns [`SecondOrderStatus::Inconclusive`] when the active constraint gradients span the whole space (no feasible direction), when the null space or the eigenproblem cannot be formed, or when the eigenvalue is inside the margin. The cost is `O(n^2)` evaluations of `f`, `h` and `g` for the Hessian (each call is counted as one evaluation), plus the finite-difference Jacobians of the constraints, and dense `O(n^3)` linear algebra.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_sequence_limit" => "Physical native series/sequence convergence. sum_series: start,max_terms,tolerance,value_scale,max_evaluations,term(Float)->E. sequence_limit omits start. Levin: max_terms,value_scale,max_evaluations,term(Int)->E; result includes native error estimate. References/tolerances are positive physical E; callback failures propagate and budgets bound actual host calls. Finds the limit of the sequence `term(0), term(1), ..., term(max_terms-1)` by applying Aitken's process repeatedly until the last two accelerated values differ by less than `tolerance`. # Errors Returns an error if a term is not finite, or if the tolerance is not reached with the given number of terms.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
    "num_native_sim_cutcell_default_depth" => "Default refinement depth for faces and cells.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_sim_dg_log_mean" => "Logarithmic mean `(a - b) / (ln a - ln b)` with a series for close arguments.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_sim_elliptic_carlson_rc" => "Carlson's degenerate integral `R_C(x, y)` (`x >= 0`, `y != 0`; `y < 0` gives the Cauchy principal value).\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_sim_elliptic_carlson_rj" => "Carlson's `R_J(x, y, z, p)` for `x, y, z >= 0` (at most one zero) and `p > 0`. Finite arguments are evaluated using homogeneity and duplication. Invalid inputs return `NaN`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_sim_elliptic_elliptic_pi" => "Incomplete elliptic integral of the third kind. `Pi(n; phi, m) = int_0^phi dt / ((1 - n sin^2 t) sqrt(1 - m sin^2 t))` for any real `phi` (`Pi(phi + j pi) = Pi(phi) + 2 j Pi(n, m)`). Continuation across whole periods requires `n < 1` and `m < 1`. A principal-interval path is real when both `n sin^2 t < 1` and `m sin^2 t < 1` throughout the interval.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_sim_elliptic_elliptic_pi_complete" => "Complete elliptic integral of the third kind `Pi(n, m)` with `n < 1`, `m < 1`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_sim_elliptic_jacobi_int_inv_sq" => "`int_0^u dv / (1 - n sn^2(v, m))^2` with `u = F(phi, m)`, in closed form (Byrd-Friedman 336.02) through `E`, `F` and `Pi`; requires `n != 1` and `n != m`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_sim_elliptic_jacobi_int_sn2" => "`int_0^u sn^2(v, m) dv` for the amplitude `phi = am(u)` (any real `phi`): `(u - E(phi, m)) / m` with `u = F(phi, m)`.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_sim_physics_cfd_cfl_number" => "Calculates the CFL (Courant-Friedrichs-Lewy) number. For stability, typically CFL ≤ 1 for explicit methods. # Arguments * `velocity` - Flow velocity (m/s) * `dt` - Time step (s) * `dx` - Grid spacing (m)\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_sim_physics_cfd_check_cfl_stability" => "Checks if the CFL condition is satisfied for stability.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_sim_physics_cfd_diffusion_number" => "Calculates the diffusion number for stability analysis. For stability, typically r ≤ 0.5 for 1D explicit diffusion.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_sim_physics_cfd_froude_number" => "Calculates the Froude number: Fr = V/√(gL) # Arguments * `velocity` - Flow velocity (m/s) * `length` - Characteristic length (m) * `gravity` - Gravitational acceleration (m/s²)\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_sim_physics_cfd_mach_number" => "Calculates the Mach number: Ma = V/c # Arguments * `velocity` - Flow velocity (m/s) * `speed_of_sound` - Speed of sound in the medium (m/s)\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_sim_physics_cfd_reynolds_number" => "Calculates the Reynolds number: Re = ρVL/μ = VL/ν # Arguments * `velocity` - Characteristic velocity (m/s) * `length` - Characteristic length (m) * `kinematic_viscosity` - Kinematic viscosity ν (m²/s)\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_sim_physics_fea_max_shear_stress" => "Computes the maximum shear stress from principal stresses.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_sim_physics_fvm_minmod" => "Minmod limiter for MUSCL reconstruction.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_sim_physics_fvm_van_leer" => "Van Leer limiter for MUSCL reconstruction.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_simulated_annealing_scaled" => "Native scaled global/constrained optimization with shared actual host evaluation limit. Nelder: x,xscale,yscale,step,tol,iterations,budget,f. Differential evolution: lo,hi,xscale,yscale,population,generations,budget,seed,f. Annealing: x,xscale,yscale,step,temperature,cooling,iterations,budget,seed,f. Constrained: x,xscale,yscale,equality_scale,inequality_scale,tol,iterations,budget,f,eq,ineq. Constraints independently carry C/H units; SQP returns physical multipliers E/C and E/H, native status and second-order verdict. Second-order: x,lambda,mu,xscale,yscale,eqscale,ineqscale,budget,f,eq,ineq. No global-optimality claim; native iteration/status semantics retained. Simulated annealing with geometric cooling and Gaussian proposals of scale `step * T / T0`-adjusted; seeded and deterministic.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
