    "num_native_spin_wang_landau_ising_d1" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Wang-Landau estimate of the Ising density of states, normalised to `sum g = 2^N`. The move set is single spin flips; the flatness criterion is `min H > flatness * mean H` over the energies visited so far; `ln f` starts at 1 and is halved until `ln_f_final`. Nearest-neighbour only (`J2 = 0`); the energy levels are those of [`Lattice::bonds`]. # Errors Propagates lattice errors.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_spin_wang_landau_ising_d2" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Wang-Landau estimate of the Ising density of states, normalised to `sum g = 2^N`. The move set is single spin flips; the flatness criterion is `min H > flatness * mean H` over the energies visited so far; `ln f` starts at 1 and is halved until `ln_f_final`. Nearest-neighbour only (`J2 = 0`); the energy levels are those of [`Lattice::bonds`]. # Errors Propagates lattice errors.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_spin_wang_landau_ising_d3" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Wang-Landau estimate of the Ising density of states, normalised to `sum g = 2^N`. The move set is single spin flips; the flatness criterion is `min H > flatness * mean H` over the energies visited so far; `ln f` starts at 1 and is halved until `ln_f_final`. Nearest-neighbour only (`J2 = 0`); the energy levels are those of [`Lattice::bonds`]. # Errors Propagates lattice errors.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_spin_wang_landau_on_d1_n1" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Wang-Landau density of states of an O(N) model with **continuous** spins on a binned energy axis `[e_min, e_max)` with `nbins` bins (moves leaving the window are rejected). Single-spin moves of width `delta`; `ln f` starts at 1 and is halved whenever the histogram of visited bins satisfies `min H > flatness * mean H` (checked every `check` attempted moves) until `ln_f_final`. Returns `(bin centre, ln g)` for the visited bins, normalised to `sum g = 1`. The model is the nearest-neighbour one (`J2 = 0`); the signature carries no coupling, so a next-nearest-neighbour run has to use [`ParallelTempering`]. # Errors Fails for invalid bins or lattice errors.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_spin_wang_landau_on_d1_n2" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Wang-Landau density of states of an O(N) model with **continuous** spins on a binned energy axis `[e_min, e_max)` with `nbins` bins (moves leaving the window are rejected). Single-spin moves of width `delta`; `ln f` starts at 1 and is halved whenever the histogram of visited bins satisfies `min H > flatness * mean H` (checked every `check` attempted moves) until `ln_f_final`. Returns `(bin centre, ln g)` for the visited bins, normalised to `sum g = 1`. The model is the nearest-neighbour one (`J2 = 0`); the signature carries no coupling, so a next-nearest-neighbour run has to use [`ParallelTempering`]. # Errors Fails for invalid bins or lattice errors.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
    "num_native_spin_wang_landau_on_d1_n3" => "Checked native method over explicitly normalized values. Session/kind, shape and work/allocation bounds are enforced. Wang-Landau density of states of an O(N) model with **continuous** spins on a binned energy axis `[e_min, e_max)` with `nbins` bins (moves leaving the window are rejected). Single-spin moves of width `delta`; `ln f` starts at 1 and is halved whenever the histogram of visited bins satisfies `min H > flatness * mean H` (checked every `check` attempted moves) until `ln_f_final`. Returns `(bin centre, ln g)` for the visited bins, normalised to `sum g = 1`. The model is the nearest-neighbour one (`J2 = 0`); the signature carries no coupling, so a next-nearest-neighbour run has to use [`ParallelTempering`]. # Errors Fails for invalid bins or lattice errors.\n\nReturns an unevaluated term; call `compute` to reduce it. Pass `checked=true` to call it with native arguments and receive a Value.",
