    "num_pde_fem_be_source_adaptive" => "Tolerance-controlled PDE evolution with explicit coordinate L, time T, and field U dimensions. Diffusivity is L^2/T; velocity L/T; reaction 1/T; Neumann U/L; Robin alpha dimensionless, beta L, gamma U. Grid/state lengths and boundary pairing/corner data are checked. Controls: t0,t1,rtol,atol,h0,h_min,h_max,max_steps,max_rejections,max_step_calls,max_evaluations. Boundary record: kind,value,flux,alpha,beta,gamma vectors (one broadcast face or two per active axis). Only accepted states are returned; step doubling controls temporal error, independently of spatial error. Optional trailing direction and dimensionless terminal-event callback; wave events receive displacement and velocity separately. FEM uses a fixed simplex mesh; source variants take a vectorized (time,coordinates)->nodal-rate callback with a consistent mass load. FVM preserves periodic/transmissive flux methods; classic LF's timestep-dependent viscosity may prevent strict temporal convergence. DG uses periodic SSPRK3 in one or two dimensions; Fourier uses ETDRK4 and a dimensioned nonlinear rate callback. Budgets and callback failures are explicit errors. Adaptive FEM heat with a serial vectorized nodal source callback. `source(t, coordinates)` returns one physical field/time value per node. Its consistent mass load is added to the problem's existing source load. # Errors Invalid source/state, theta/controls, callback errors or failed linear solve.\n\nReturns a dynamic value: this operator is higher-order, its function parameters are host callbacks, and a callable passed for one is registered with the signature the operator declares.",
